{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far","id":1284756,"title":"Third Edition in Retrospect, Thus Far","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-04T10:38:20-08:00","id":1284756,"title":"Third Edition in Retrospect, Thus Far","content":"I've had some experience running a Third Edition Exalted game now, and I've had some time away from that game to reflect on what I really liked about how this edition has done things, and what I would have liked to see done differently. Things that have made my game better, and things that made my game worse.<br /> <br /> Pros<br /> 1) The combat system was fairly intuitive for the players to pick up on. Not all of them exactly liked it, but that's because said player is a Pathfinder/D&amp;D 3.5 system junkie who self-admittedly values mechanics over 'make believe'. For the rest of them, it was easy enough to dig into the base mechanics and play around with them to satisfaction.<br /> <br /> 2) The setting as it exists right now has just enough interesting things for me to poke at and flesh out on my own that I was able to get players invested in building the world around them up. Not a lot of people made Lore rolls to do so unfortunately since it's so counter to how every other RPG we've ever played did it, but we made some good use of it anyway. <br /> <br /> 3) It did a great job of making the players feel empowered to take on whatever it is they built their characters to do well, right out the gate. <br /> <br /> Cons<br /> 1) Solar Charms are a bloated mess to maneuver through. Individual Charms feel like they don't do a lot on their own, and require building along with a bunch of others to do so. This by itself wouldn't be all that bad, but it dramatically slowed down play when everyone had to keep referring back to the book to figure out how to play their characters even when we all knew how the base mechanics worked. Eventually I just got to copy-pasting Charms out of the book to reference them more easily.<br /> <br /> 2) Evocations. I love the idea of Evocations, of Artifacts with their own super special unique custom powers, but the reality of it all has just made a mess for me. The pre-created Evocation trees in the books are great, and I've made use of them as much as I can, but when one of your players is a Twilight Caste with Craft Supernal who is doing their utmost best to (and mechanically, can) churn Artifacts out and has a bunch of ideas for what they want the things to do I'm busy hitting my head against a desk. It's gotten to the point where I would have preferred we just be given a nice, clean, universally applicable point-build system to design effects for Artifacts with. It would lose a lot of the flavor of Evocations, but it would be much more playable for my group than what we have.<br /> <br /> 3) A deficit of things to throw against my players. Recent supplemental pieces have alleviated much of this issue, but back when we just had the Corebook I was hankering for a Monster Manual to throw at my players.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I'll think of others later, but this is what came to mind while I'm sick at home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T10:49:48-08:00","id":1284761,"title":"","content":"Pro:<br /> Love the setting more then ever.<br /> Combat system is fun!<br /> Charms!<br /> <br /> Con:<br /> Can\u2019t have quick simple combat anymore, it is now always an investment of time.<br /> Can\u2019t have one off Strikes. Like in game we wanted to have someone way up the SPSitV user and have him Strike with his blade because he wakes up on guard but we had no rules for doing that since combat is no longer simulationist, not it\u2019s more videogamy in its abstraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T10:59:00-08:00","id":1284764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284761#post1284761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u2019t have quick simple combat anymore, it is now always an investment of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seriously never had a simple quick combat in 2e that wasn't against something 3e would just designate as a trivial opponent, and let you kill with a single roll. If a 2e opponent was worth rolling dice against, it almost invariably took 4+ hours, even if the fight ended in less than thirty seconds in-character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T11:19:39-08:00","id":1284770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284761#post1284761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u2019t have one off Strikes. Like in game we wanted to have someone way up the SPSitV user and have him Strike with his blade because he wakes up on guard but we had no rules for doing that since combat is no longer simulationist, not it\u2019s more videogamy in its abstraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not clear what you mean by 'One off Strike' in this context; could you clarify?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T11:49:12-08:00","id":1284777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284770#post1284770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not clear what you mean by 'One off Strike' in this context; could you clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean a simple roll one attack. Like the example I gave a swordsman was sleeping and he is trained to strike if his sleep is disturbed as a survival thing. I can\u2019t quite do that now because combat doesn\u2019t work that way with initiative. The closest I can get is to use his wake up strike using the Trap rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T11:51:52-08:00","id":1284780,"title":"","content":"Oh heck... let's see..<br /> <br /> Pros:<br /> <br /> 1) Ex3 has the best iteration of the setting so far.<br /> 2) The idea of witherings and decisives is cool...<br /> 3) Weapon categories are way better than having separate stats for a knife, a kukri dagger and a karambit.<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> <br /> 1) Ex3 needs a ton of micro-managing to play: mote regeneration, onslaught penalties, number of turns in crash, crash reversal bonuses, double 6s if..., keep track of your anima level, aura, shifting initiatives, relative rangebands between characters to determine pools and penalties... etc etc etc... As an adult, I simply don't have enough time to master all of these things, so I keep breaking rules and playing as well as posible, but never exactly by the rules<br /> <br /> 2) There are no solar level antagonists... and you can't always bring a deathlord to every session unless you have some sort of he-man skeletor relation... or some crap like that.<br /> <br /> 3) I don't get why gaining momentum and advantage towards an enemy lets me throw a powerful decisive attack to another enemy over which I hold no tactical advantage... I may be playing it wrong I don't know, see #1 of this list.<br /> <br /> 4) Ex3, the book, is messy... too big, too many charms... I don't like it very much.<br /> <br /> I really really REALLY hope that the new devs get the chance to write and put out a lighter version of Ex3 (I recall one of them mentioning something similar to that). The game is amazing, but there are lots of things that could be polished. I'd definitely pay for a new set of rules or add ons that could make the game easier to run, like in Ex1 when that included the famous power combat in the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> *Starts praying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 02-04-2019, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T12:05:17-08:00","id":1284783,"title":"","content":"Should we list problems if they were also problems for us in 2e and just kind of carried over? Or just pro-con about the changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T12:08:21-08:00","id":1284785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284764#post1284764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seriously never had a simple quick combat in 2e that wasn't against something 3e would just designate as a trivial opponent, and let you kill with a single roll. If a 2e opponent was worth rolling dice against, it almost invariably took 4+ hours, even if the fight ended in less than thirty seconds in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of beings that can hurt you but you can crumple in one blow, like a lot of animals.<br /> <br /> And not all combats are to the death. The example I gave isn\u2019t really serious combat but it\u2019s a story bit to complicate things with a bloody wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T12:35:31-08:00","id":1284789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284783#post1284783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we list problems if they were also problems for us in 2e and just kind of carried over? Or just pro-con about the changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the problem carried over, I think 'Them carrying this problem over is causing problems' is a fair thing to note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T12:58:40-08:00","id":1284790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284777#post1284777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean a simple roll one attack. Like the example I gave a swordsman was sleeping and he is trained to strike if his sleep is disturbed as a survival thing. I can\u2019t quite do that now because combat doesn\u2019t work that way with initiative. The closest I can get is to use his wake up strike using the Trap rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only difference I see between 2e and 3e for that example would be rolling initiative for the sleeping guy before making the attack. Is that what you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T14:59:22-08:00","id":1284810,"title":"","content":"Oh... does Mr. Negative over here join this little shindig? *sigh* Might as well. Let's see<br /> <br /> Pros<br /> #1: Balanced, workable engine that doesn't rely on houserules or errata<br /> #2: Interesting new mechanical ideas, like the withering/decisive split, the Aura system or Introduce a Fact<br /> <br /> Cons<br /> #1: Combat is slooooow. It can get molasses level when opponents are roughly evenly matched. Fights haven't given me the same air of excitement or memorability as 2e did, and encounter balance is hard to eyeball. Shoutout to my poor Storyteller who has had a fair share of what looked like potential recurring villains die really frecking early.<br /> #2: Every single setting change, bar 'remove obviously gross thing', was for the worse. Yes, <i>all of them.</i> I only put this on the list because, while it's subjective, the fact that the setting is so different from the way I like it makes it really annoying to ST: it's hard to lay down changed fluff to players who're jumping on board now and don't have the older books.<br /> #3: How much stuff is left in the Storyteller's hands? Evocations, the Leadership system, difficulties on rolls... while freedom for the ST is appreciated, giving a baseline to work from in some of these situations would've been really helpful.<br /> #4: Craft is a bloated gnarled tree that needs to be cut down, and is counter to immersive play<br /> #5: Charm bloat make the system really hard to approach for new players. Even for those used to it, the sheer number of charms gets kinda ridiculous. Didn't people used to make fun of DotFA NPCs for having full page charm lists?<br /> <br /> *sigh* Weirdly, while this list is stacked negative, I'm optimistic about where the line goes from here? Most of these are just problems I had with Core that haven't gone away. Dragon Blooded hasn't changed my overall feelings towards Ex3 as it stands, but it's sold me on this dev team, and I'm looking forward a lot to the Storyteller's Guide for mechanical advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T17:17:32-08:00","id":1284854,"title":"","content":"I think we had very similar experiences with Ex3 Croakamancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T17:41:14-08:00","id":1284859,"title":"","content":"Oh, another weird con that's very exclusive to Solars but that stood out to me in my game.<br /> <br /> 4) The decision to exclude Sorcery from the usual 'You get to take everything up to Essence 5 in your Supernal' way of doing things. We had an Eclipse Caste with Occult Supernal who wanted to be the world's greatest sorcerer, kinda like the Twilight Caste was the World's Greatest Craftsman and the Night was the World's Greatest Horseman, but they couldn't be. Oh they were probably better at the first circle of sorcery than anyone else could be with how they were built, but by the time the game stopped they never got a chance to use the second circle at all.<br /> <br /> It's especially sad, because while I'm going back I'd say the sorcery systems are definitely one of the pros of the game otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T20:14:25-08:00","id":1284880,"title":"","content":"Mortals can actually interact with the mechanics meaningfully now.<br /> <br /> While it might not be what many want from this system and this title, *most* of the issues posted so far in this thread effectively go away once you stop playing Exalted and start playing mortals. Im not kidding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T20:29:45-08:00","id":1284882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284859#post1284859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, another weird con that's very exclusive to Solars but that stood out to me in my game.<br /> <br /> 4) The decision to exclude Sorcery from the usual 'You get to take everything up to Essence 5 in your Supernal' way of doing things. We had an Eclipse Caste with Occult Supernal who wanted to be the world's greatest sorcerer, kinda like the Twilight Caste was the World's Greatest Craftsman and the Night was the World's Greatest Horseman, but they couldn't be. Oh they were probably better at the first circle of sorcery than anyone else could be with how they were built, but by the time the game stopped they never got a chance to use the second circle at all.<br /> <br /> It's especially sad, because while I'm going back I'd say the sorcery systems are definitely one of the pros of the game otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because it would otherwise take only three starting Charm slots to become capable of melting cities from the word go. That's both a much shorter path than any other Supernal needs, and kind of has a more profound impact than any Supernal besides Lore (which is a lot more restricted in mass destruction than sorcery is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T20:41:57-08:00","id":1284884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284859#post1284859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The decision to exclude Sorcery from the usual 'You get to take everything up to Essence 5 in your Supernal' way of doing things. We had an Eclipse Caste with Occult Supernal who wanted to be the world's greatest sorcerer, kinda like the Twilight Caste was the World's Greatest Craftsman and the Night was the World's Greatest Horseman, but they couldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that a starting Solar who has Ride Supernal isn't necessarily the world's premiere mistress of horses, even if she starts out with fifteen Ride Charms. If she wants to be called the greatest rider in the world, she's gotta, y'know, <i>do stuff</i>, same as the guy who wants to be the greatest sorcerer.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd likewise be hesitant to call a Twilight &quot;the World's Greatest Craftsman&quot; before he's so much as created an artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-05-2019, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T00:16:11-08:00","id":1284898,"title":"","content":"It's time to make... a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cmP5fSQGzUQ\" target=\"_blank\">pro-con sandwich</a>.<br /> <br /> My experience is I played and ran countless games of 2e, and have played in 4 campaigns of 3e, where I ST'd exactly half of them. Also a few test sessions with DBs.<br /> <br /> <b>Pro </b>- Combat System: The new combat system is pretty good. It gives exciting cinematic combat, with a good safety net for new players, while at the same time keeping the same 2e more realistic wounding/healing. It also gives a lot of neat tactical options, reduced lethality, and gave some good scaffolding to link charms to.<br /> <br /> <b>Con </b>- Most other Systems: The crafting system isn't so bad, although Solar craft kind of just breaks it further. The naval combat system isn't totally bad, but it suffers a lot from having absolutely no worthy foes for the Solar to fight. I've found the social system to be a bit too complex and kind of obscure, at least at first. I think I get it better now but I'm still wary about using it properly with like decision points and stuff. Leadership is also not super well defined, not many examples or guidelines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pro </b>- Better Balance: In my last campaign of 2e I played a Dawn battle hydra, which isn't even remotely the most powerful kind of Dawn, and near the end of the campaign a circle of high essence DB martial arts masters showed up. I raised my eyebrow at my ST and he assured me that we wouldn't waste any time rolling it out. So we went from that to a point where if you had 5 immaculate DB grand masters versus even a whole circle of essence 2 Solars, there's a fight there. That combat balance style also applies all over the place with stuff like social settings and even athletics style feats, it's definitely better. <br /> <br /> <b>Con </b>- Some Exalts Still Too Big: That being said, I often have problems working between what the game seems to suggest and what my players are often capable of. I've very often been left with really unsatisfying scenes where at the climax of an epic arc the antagonist gets unceremoniously dumped on, in either combat or social or some other merit like a horse race or something. I have no problem with my players being awesome and smashing through many challenges with the ease that you would expect from epic heroes, but sometimes it's still too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pro </b>- I like basically all the changes to the setting. Lunars feel more capable and diverse, Dragonblooded feel less chumpy, the split between the near and far north is good.<br /> <br /> <b>Con </b>- The Solar charmset in particular feels a bit bloated, and some of the charms feel oddly specific in their application. I believe the point was that there would not need to be any supplement books after the corebook to augment Solar charms, which is admirable, but it does mean that there is a lot to grind through.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pro </b>- I think evocations are cool and actually fairly well executed. They're exactly the right space for a developer or player to say &quot;I had a cool idea for X little thing.&quot; that isn't really wide enough in applicability to put into a charmset, and/or has more to do with an item than personal abilities. Later evocations tend to work more smoothly than corebook ones,m though.<br /> <br /> <b>Con </b>- Supernals, while great at what they are supposed to do, can kind of ruin the feeling of character progression. It's not really a problem so much as a trap to fall into, if that even matters to you, but if you take too much right off the hop, you'll not really become a much better X as you gain xp, but just get better at other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pro </b>- Dragonblooded Book: I'm bias of course, but I really liked how they made great houses feel like distinct factions, like running a Ledal game actually makes sense, not just a Dynasty game. Also their charms put them in range for me to do a lot better with the NPCs and guidelines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully sometime soon I can get a proper DB game in, and see if my gut feeling is right, or if there's hidden problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T02:32:26-08:00","id":1284906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284854#post1284854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we had very similar experiences with Ex3 Croakamancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm... we're at a similar point though we took different paths to get here. You praise the setting as best take so far, I spent weeks upon discovering the edition in progress ranting at almost every quote about the setting in What We Know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I take your point.<br /> <br /> Reading this thread is interesting, especially the number of people praising combat. I'm wondering how my experience here is so different from the norm, and will try and rethink my approach a bit. Kinda stand by what I said for the moment though: rocket tag has a ton of downsides, but if you aren't just twinking and optimising Ex2 could get visceral, immediate, tense and exciting. I stand by this one memory of a fight that had me on the edge of my seat. Ex3... the withering/decisive split makes moments like that <i>way </i>harder to do. And that's a shame. The engine is fun, but it's tough to get it to 'exciting'<br /> <br /> *hums* I'd kinda be down for a Power Combat variant in the STG. Maybe make all withering attacks against a crashed target do direct damage - like a Battle Group? *hums* May wanna spin this out into a thread later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T07:25:46-08:00","id":1284960,"title":"","content":"I frankly don't understand the complaints that you can't have sudden, visceral, lethal combat in 3E. Even without taking into account Trivial opponents or treating NPCs as a size 0 battle group, my players have, on numerous occasions, decimated opponents round one.<br /> <br /> Its not hard at all to crack 7 initiative turn one, and there's tons of things that futz around with the Join Battle roll to get well in excess of it. That can set you up with enough dice to kill most things that aren't fellow empowered beings or critters with Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> Thrown and stealth are both very good at laying insane amounts of first action hurt on someone, and my Brawler Eclipse caste riding limit break dropped the five ox-body Dawn straight into Incap with a single punch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T08:14:56-08:00","id":1284968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284960#post1284960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I frankly don't understand the complaints that you can't have sudden, visceral, lethal combat in 3E. Even without taking into account Trivial opponents or treating NPCs as a size 0 battle group, my players have, on numerous occasions, decimated opponents round one.<br /> <br /> Its not hard at all to crack 7 initiative turn one, and there's tons of things that futz around with the Join Battle roll to get well in excess of it. That can set you up with enough dice to kill most things that aren't fellow empowered beings or critters with Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> Thrown and stealth are both very good at laying insane amounts of first action hurt on someone, and my Brawler Eclipse caste riding limit break dropped the five ox-body Dawn straight into Incap with a single punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, what was that whole thing about 'mortals totally matter now'? :P<br /> <br /> Yeah, you can eliminate trivial opponents fairly quickly, even if you don't use the rules entitled that. My complaint is more trying to create a sorta excitement/sudden fear/despair in PCs, evoking that key moment when things could turn around against them. If a fight in Ex3 turns against the PCs, it's gonna be a slow grind down as they struggle to claw some initiative back. It's much harder to get that one sharp, shocking moment, that one key attack. Because any key attack has to be preceeded by one, if not more withering attacks, or possible a strong Awareness roll. I miss the feeling that every blow matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T08:47:16-08:00","id":1284972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284968#post1284968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, what was that whole thing about 'mortals totally matter now'? :P<br /> <br /> Yeah, you can eliminate trivial opponents fairly quickly, even if you don't use the rules entitled that. My complaint is more trying to create a sorta excitement/sudden fear/despair in PCs, evoking that key moment when things could turn around against them. If a fight in Ex3 turns against the PCs, it's gonna be a slow grind down as they struggle to claw some initiative back. It's much harder to get that one sharp, shocking moment, that one key attack. Because any key attack has to be preceeded by one, if not more withering attacks, or possible a strong Awareness roll. I miss the feeling that every blow matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hitting an initiative shift (which is pretty doable when you hit someone in Crash with a decisive and get reset) creates that feeling pretty effectively, IMO. As can Clash attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T09:25:18-08:00","id":1284979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284968#post1284968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, what was that whole thing about 'mortals totally matter now'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still on the table. Not all mortals will be trivial opponents, and not all trivial opponents will be mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T10:28:19-08:00","id":1284998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284972#post1284972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hitting an initiative shift (which is pretty doable when you hit someone in Crash with a decisive and get reset) creates that feeling pretty effectively, IMO. As can Clash attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I generally find that, or to a lesser extent with Initiative Breaks.<br /> <br /> People jump from Crash or a few initiative to loads of initiative, while their enemy drops from a significant amount into Crash.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed that I thought was interesting, was that I ran a number of fights where it felt to me that the PCs were never in any significant danger, as none of them actually took any damage. But the players felt they were in danger, sometimes even fleeing (I never saw anyone flee in 2nd ed), because they went into Crash and their enemies got lots of initiative.<br /> <br /> I know that to me, as ST, players using Heavenly Guardian Defence felt unassailable... but to the players they didn't, because they kept running out of initiative.<br /> <br /> So it seemed to create the feeling of back-and-forth tension and danger without actually doing any damage to the PCs. Which is rather different, and I think kind of good in terms of enjoyment (it's a bit complicated).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, one thing I'm finding interesting reading this thread, like Croakamancer mentioned, is how different people's experiences of the same game have been.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My complaint is more trying to create a sorta excitement/sudden fear/despair in PCs, evoking that key moment when things could turn around against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get this a lot more with 3rd ed than with 2nd, where perfect-spam leached out the excitement... or suddenly out of nowhere PCs died (I can think of at least three times that PCs killed other PCs without meaning to, to everyone's surprise).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The combat system was fairly intuitive for the players to pick up on.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players found it quite unintuitive. They're used to it now, but it took a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but when one of your players is a Twilight Caste with Craft Supernal who is doing their utmost best to (and mechanically, can) churn Artifacts out and has a bunch of ideas</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been disappointed with how few artefacts crafters have made. In fact, I regret taking Craft on one character, and really regret taking it with another character. Almost a total waste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u2019t have quick simple combat anymore, it is now always an investment of time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat is slooooow. It can get molasses level when opponents are roughly evenly matched.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find combat very quick, but it's significantly faster than 2nd ed. About the same as DnD, and more interesting. And I suspect it'd be faster if I wasn't playing such high-xp games where the players can't remember all their charms well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) The decision to exclude Sorcery from the usual 'You get to take everything up to Essence 5 in your Supernal' way of doing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, this was a very good decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think evocations are cool and actually fairly well executed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree... but the thing is, I'm just generally not very interested in magic weapons.<br /> I got Arms of Chosen, and basically felt it was a well-written book with a lot of good ideas... that I just wasn't very interested in.<br /> I liked some of the weirder ones, like Asphodel or Gorgon, but most of them, as far as I was concerned, were just another combat tree, and there's plenty of combat trees as-is.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's stuff others have said that I agree with too, of course. The Solar charmset is too bloated, Supernals can eliminate character progression as a kind of trap (though I think the character gen that lets you take a rating of 5 dots in seven different abilities already kind of does that), there's too much management (motes, wp, resets, onslaught, initiative, Aura, etc), the changes to the Dragonblood house fluff is good (to my surprise; I thought I'd hate it, but I don't), the combat system is good, the social system is good but a bit difficult, etc.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not saying &quot;you guys are wrong!&quot; Just that a lot of stuff seems to be things people have quite different experiences of, and I think that's weird, but also interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> One final thing:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get why gaining momentum and advantage towards an enemy lets me throw a powerful decisive attack to another enemy over which I hold no tactical advantage... I may be playing it wrong I don't know, see #1 of this list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, that's how the rules work.<br /> It's kind of weird. I had great fun harvesting initiative off a mortal guard who thought he was trapping me until his Dawn boss arrived, and then I hit the Dawn for a 52-dice damage roll. I think the Dawn's player was a bit irritated though, because it's kind of stupid.<br /> <br /> But I think it probably works like that because a)it comes up less than you'd expect, and b)tracking it seperately for each character would be a big hassle. And Exalted already has enough stuff to track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-05-2019, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T10:29:33-08:00","id":1285000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284880#post1284880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *most* of the issues posted so far in this thread effectively go away once you stop playing Exalted and start playing mortals. Im not kidding</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you. TBH, that's like 2nd ed. Most of the problems people complained about in 2nd ed went away if you played a mortal game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-05-2019, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T10:45:01-08:00","id":1285001,"title":"","content":"So, my own quick pro-con list...<br /> <br /> Pros:<ul><li>The combat system,</li> <li>certain Solar charm trees (Investigation, Occult and Larceny are big improvements from 2nd ed),</li> <li>the DB and Arms charmsets</li> <li>the changes to fluff and new locations (though sometimes I think the lack of magitech robs something unique about Exalted)</li> <li>the rules for antagonists, such as spirits and monsters.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Cons:<ul><li>Character gen,</li> <li>certain Solar charm trees (Athletics, Craft and Presence being the worst),</li> <li>the movement rules,</li> <li>the sheer number of charms (both in the charmset, and that you start with),</li> <li>the complexity of the game (which is connected to the number of charms, but not entirely; I liked the ideas of the social system, for example, but in practice it's been a bit too complex for most of the social PCs to really engage with.</li> <li>the lack of high-level antagonists.</li> </ul><br /> A couple of these may not be as bad at low-XP play (presumably 15 charms plus excellencies is easy to keep track of), I don't know, but they're problematic at the high-XP I've been playing/running (40 charms plus excellencies is definitely not easy to keep track of).<br /> <br /> The Dragonblood charm set and Evocations are much better than the Solar charmset (though the DB one is a bit fiddly for less mechanically-minded players), so I'm optimistic for upcoming books. Hundred Devils Night Parade has generally been quite good, though I'd like more high-powered stuff.<br /> Adversaries of the Righteous is similar; I really don't care about mortal NPCs, and even something like the Exigent was interesting but way too weak to be very useful. They're not badly written, I just need more powerful stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-05-2019, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T12:04:34-08:00","id":1285026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285000#post1285000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe you. TBH, that's like 2nd ed. Most of the problems people complained about in 2nd ed went away if you played a mortal game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll second that, I actually ran a 5th campaign that I neglected to mention. It was short, 3-4 sessions, and amaaazing. My mortal PCs battled exalted foes, ancient monsters, flew daring airship chases, it was great. It\u2019s hard to compare apples to oranges but it\u2019s one of my favourite campaigns so far I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also as to edge of the seat combat, I also have to say 3rd edition does it more for me than second. In second edition perfects and flurry breakers and stuff makes a large chunk of fighting boring. In third edition though I\u2019ve had countless times where one of two big bad guys got annihilated by our dawn, only to have the other bad guy hammer him into crash and pick up 30 initiative. Then everyone at the table gets that \u201coh shiiit\u201d look when they realize that if she lands that next decisive hit, they\u2019re dead. Then it\u2019s a desperate struggle to get her initiative down before she lands it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to mortals mattering, I\u2019d say they do, but in specific ways and times. Like I said, I think this system is way better than last edition although not quite where I\u2019d want it. Most average mortals, like with 2s in their stats, are nothing, even in a battlegroup. The most they usually do there is rack up an onslaught penalty. Where they ARE useful though, is as big mortal heroes, combined with supernatural foes and/or battle groups. If your big bad Abyssal has a powerful mortal lieutenant in command of a battlegroup of 100 archers who are peppering your entire fight with arrows, they\u2019re something you have to deal with. Without sorcery, that usually means wasting a decisive on the mortal and at least one somewhat fruitless withering against the battlegroup. If you don\u2019t they could pretty reasonably get an AoE attack with like 16+ dice to hit against most of your party. Their damage will probably be low enough that the heavy armor people will get chipped at and have an onslaught penalty rack up, where the softer members are going to have to spend motes not to get hit or actually take reasonable damage.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not a total game changer, but it does technically matter, where in 2e with Infinite Melee Excellency up they could be ignored to absolutely no detriment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I should also add we houseruled battlegroups to only give one initiative break per attack even if they get dropped more than one magnitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-05-2019, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T12:25:45-08:00","id":1285032,"title":"","content":"Not really an exhaustive list on either side, but:<br /> <br /> Pro:<br /> -DBs actually feel like Exalts<br /> -Combat is not perfect-spam<br /> -Social system has texture without being a combat analogue<br /> -Most setting changes<br /> -The idea, if not execution, of Evocations<br /> -Lunars have a role in the setting<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> -Crafting <br /> -Needing to homebrew charm trees to make Artifacts worth it and, for some characters, to have a useful outlet for half your XP - and not getting a system to help people who aren't good at homebrew (yet) <br /> -Crafting<br /> -Transferability of momentum (but I'm not sure how to make a comprehensible fix)<br /> -Really dull fights between high soak opponents<br /> -Deprecating magitech<br /> -Crafting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T13:11:33-08:00","id":1285046,"title":"","content":"I agree with a lot of that.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit uncertain about the magitech.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, sometimes 3rd edition seemed like it was just Magitech, Magitech, Magitech, especially when playing Dragonblood (most of us had Magitech armour, because it was so much better than normal artefact armour). And it kind of detracted from everything else; it seemed like the magitech setting, rather than the Wuxia-Anime-Classical Mythology setting.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I started playing DnD again a year or two ago, and I used to play a lot of Qin (the Wuxia game about ancient China). Magitech, essentially, is one of the things that is very distinct about Exalted.<br /> (And FFVI is one of my favourite ever games.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Crafting... I thought Crafting was a terrible mess when I first read it. Then later I realised that maybe the issue was the Solar charms. The DB charms seem much less broken.<br /> I know some people have found the Craft system very good.<br /> And then I tried actually playing a Solar crafter myself (twice), and I found it a)dull, and b)not worth the XP cost of all those charms. Though I went with the XP-generation charm tree (as crafters I saw before were chronically short of craft XP) and I've seen people on this forum call it a trap.<br /> <br /> I think maybe it could be good with a very different charmset. DB craft is better written, but... well, I found Solar craft not worth the XP, and DB charms are weaker, so... We'll see what Lunar craft is like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really dull fights between high soak opponents</div> </div> </div> </div>All but one PC I've played/played alongside has had low soak and high damage (most of them had artefact weapons or used Brawl, hardly any had even regular armour, let alone artefact armour).<br /> The one guy with (very, very) high soak I did have a fun fight with, but I had high damage, so I guess it balances.<br /> <br /> I can imagine fights between high-soak opponents are dull, since presumably damage is very slow, but I've not seen it myself.<br /> <br /> But then, I remember when the two soak-and-regen-build Full Moons in my 2nd ed game fought each other.<br /> It took ages and ages, and went nowhere. So dull. They kept doing 1 or 2 damage, then regenerating it.<br /> <br /> In the end, I just said &quot;you fight for a whole day then drop from exhaustion.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, at least it's no worse than the old edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T14:44:47-08:00","id":1285060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285046#post1285046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with a lot of that.<br /> I think maybe it could be good with a very different charmset. DB craft is better written, but... well, I f <span style=\"color:#252423\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">why does he look twice as old as </span></span></span> ound Solar craft not worth the XP, and DB charms are weaker, so... We'll see what Lunar craft is like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have hope for this, mostly because quite a few DB craft charms either do things in addition to acting with the craft system, or are just outside of it. Like supplementing demolition, generating unexpected bonus traits, or making their final art piece act as a social influence roll. That last one I might even homebrew an essence 5 upgrade or something where the effect doesn't go away after a few days. That way you can have an awesome warship from the Shogunate that just exudes fear, or maybe pride.<br /> <br /> Also it might do the thing that many of the systems do and become more workable when a Solar isn't driving the Solar bulldozer through them. Supreme Perfection of Craft is the reason both crafters in the games I played in stopped even counting points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T15:19:05-08:00","id":1285066,"title":"","content":"Pros: <br /> <br /> -No raping pens, rape brothels, Yozi rape orgies, Infernal raping contests, or Nexus rape districts.<br /> -I can actually run the system without tearing my hair out.<br /> -Lunar dominions.<br /> -The Dreaming Sea.<br /> -The less said about Halta in previous editions, the better.<br /> -The fuckin' artwork, man.<br /> -Castes mean something.<br /> -Human beings don't get treated like interchangeable cogs in a machine the second I want to run an organization or kingdom.<br /> -Craft rules that actually incentivize me to craft.<br /> -Intimacies are important.<br /> -No Virtues to min-max for best mote-to-compulsion ratio.<br /> -The Distaff.<br /> -Liminals.<br /> -Exigents.<br /> -Getimians.<br /> -The Niobraran conflict.<br /> -The Caul.<br /> -Social scenes no longer feel like skeevy brainwashing unless you specifically build your character that way.<br /> -Solar XP.<br /> -More than two Martial Arts Styles in the Core.<br /> -More than four Stealth Charms in the Core.<br /> -More than enough Dodge Charms in the Core.<br /> -More than enough Socialize Charms in the Core.<br /> -More than enough Craft Charms in the Core.<br /> -More than enough Brawl Charms in the Core.<br /> -The Realm can meaningfully oppose Solars.<br /> -The Guild can meaningfully oppose Solars.<br /> -Sidereals can meaningfully oppose Solars.<br /> -Lunars can meaningfully oppose Solars.<br /> -Dragon-Blooded can meaningfully oppose Solars.<br /> -Sorcerers can meaningfully oppose Solars.<br /> -Mortals can meaningfully oppose Solars.<br /> -Young Solars can meaningfully oppose elder Solars.<br /> -A PC who isn't built for combat can never be accidentally killed by the ST who understands the combat system.<br /> -The Orichalcum Rule.<br /> -The Red Rule.<br /> -Being old no longer implies that an Exalt will have hundreds or thousands of XP.<br /> -Artifacts feel unique and powerful.<br /> -You no longer need a magical base of operations you may or may not care about just to have a hearthstone.<br /> -Sorcerous workings.<br /> -Sorcerous initiations.<br /> -Starting at Essence 1 and being unable to buy it higher at chargen makes actually getting to 5 feel pretty damned meaningful.<br /> -&quot;This Evocation unlocks for free when\u2026&quot;<br /> -Karvara.<br /> -Great Curse mechanics more in keeping with how the setting's presented it.<br /> <br /> Cons: <br /> -It feels pretty irksome at times to go on forums and see people bad-mouthing the very aspects you're praising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-05-2019, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T15:53:37-08:00","id":1285069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285066#post1285066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cons: <br /> -It feels pretty irksome at times to go on forums and see people bad-mouthing the very aspects you're praising.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the life of the 2e fan ^^ *passes drink*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T16:21:31-08:00","id":1285073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285032#post1285032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really an exhaustive list on either side, but:<br /> <br /> Pro:<br /> -DBs actually feel like Exalts<br /> -Combat is not perfect-spam<br /> -Social system has texture without being a combat analogue<br /> -Most setting changes<br /> -The idea, if not execution, of Evocations<br /> -Lunars have a role in the setting<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> -Crafting<br /> -Needing to homebrew charm trees to make Artifacts worth it and, for some characters, to have a useful outlet for half your XP - and not getting a system to help people who aren't good at homebrew (yet)<br /> -Crafting<br /> -Transferability of momentum (but I'm not sure how to make a comprehensible fix)<br /> -Really dull fights between high soak opponents<br /> -Deprecating magitech<br /> -Crafting</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with these but I will also add that I think the supernal keyword sucks. Exalted pretends it's supposed to be about underdogs but the characters don't start out as underdogs as they have everything they need to be king at something from start. In addition, there are more issues with the charmset than just crafting . Persona charms are unusable until you have hundreds of xp. They also do too much and at the same time too little. I get what they were going for but it does not work at all I spent several sessions of my game trying but it was bad. There are also a couple more trees that are just gross or underwhelming in practice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T17:25:36-08:00","id":1285084,"title":"","content":"I don't think Exalted comes even remotely close to pretending the characters are anything but god-kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T17:47:19-08:00","id":1285086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285073#post1285073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Persona charms are unusable until you have hundreds of xp. They also do too much and at the same time too little. I get what they were going for but it does not work at all I spent several sessions of my game trying but it was bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you want to use them for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T20:42:31-08:00","id":1285116,"title":"","content":"I'd call the combat system both a pro and a con, for me. That's why I was inspired to try my hand improving it with Momentum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Definitely, out of being deeply impressed with where it was going and what it was trying to do.<br /> <br /> In the pro side, the intent of the cinematic combat is the most innovative gaming idea I've seen in a long time. Once my gaming group and I chewed through the rules enough to see the intent and the motion in the system, it really was a perception changer. We started noticing the features of, for instance, kung-fu movies in Ex3 terminology.... that was a withering stunt, this was a decisive attack, that other was an interesting gambit.<br /> <br /> On the con side, the combat system has a lot.... a loooooot of extraneous things to deal with. Every time somebody takes an action, somebody (probably the ST, who's already really busy) has to come out of the action, then do accurate arithmetic, then do accurate sorting and bypassing to choose the next combatant. If the arithmetic is wrong, the person doing the arithmetic, sort, bypass probably has to drop everything out of their head and back up several steps to start over. There are numbers of turns (such as being crashed) to track. There are effects that adjust your turn order overriding the turn order you've just reckoned out. There is a major combat subsystem (Gambits/Decisives) that disregards a major game mechanic (double 10s for everything) and also has a -1 (cost of a Gambit in Initiative points) to continually forget. Not to mention keeping up with dice tricks (roll a yahtzee of successes to trigger a Charm), Essence for everybody and Health for everybody. <br /> <br /> A normal human can keep track of seven things in short-term memory, +- about three. The core combat system goes way beyond that for any but the very simplest of combats, so the entire time you're at it, you'll have to keep on looking things up, re-reckoning them, or recalling them.... and the combat system completely hits the rocks and comes to a halt.<br /> <br /> That sounds like it's weighed on the cons, but it really isn't, at least for me. I'm trying to be specific about the cons here, because we'd have never crunched through them or ironed them out if not for the fantastically innovated and cinematic idea underpinning combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A few other things I've liked but not seen mentioned: I really like that you can get an XP award for setting up your friends to rock the Scene. I also like the new stunting system and Essence economy. <br /> <br /> I like that there's a way to introduce facts. <br /> <br /> There was another game that came out a few years ago - I forget the name unfortunately - that was built around a system like that. The really innovative thing about that particular game was that the GM started off with a list of facts about some mystery or other, to which the players are not privy. The players would be introduced to the situation, and through the course of using their skills and descriptions, write in their own facts. The more of their own facts they prove, the more they rewrite the truth of the story and ultimately the more XP/mojo points they would be awarded.<br /> <br /> I mention that game because I can't help but feel that Abilities like Lore, Investigation, Craft, Occult, perhaps even Survival or Bureaucracy, should have some sort of unifying system underpinning them all together. The Storyteller would know the facts (or the challenges) of the situation, and by using those Abilities the character could introduce facts (or overcome challenges, or create a crafted solution) to overcome whatever obstacle. <br /> <br /> Where combat has a plethora of Abilities that all interact, and social has Abilities and its own system, braining your way to a solution seems to just vary widely from &quot;glad I knew that&quot; to a multi-tiered system with its own system of XP and project slots that's not similar to anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Your Monkey Leap distance may vary. I'm having a lot of fun though!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T20:50:08-08:00","id":1285117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285073#post1285073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Persona charms are unusable until you have hundreds of xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a person playing an Eclipse that started with persona Charms, I respectfully disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T00:29:36-08:00","id":1285143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285116#post1285116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A normal human can keep track of seven things in short-term memory, +- about three. The core combat system goes way beyond that for any but the very simplest of combats, so the entire time you're at it, you'll have to keep on looking things up, re-reckoning them, or recalling them.... and the combat system completely hits the rocks and comes to a halt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should also mention that our group had major problems with this as well until we came up with physical solutions, so that should factor into my pro/cons. A particularly crafty member of our group, like in real life, build a little board with moveable tiles and a big double-wide number line for initiative. Now whenever we go into combat a tile with each of our names on it goes onto the board and a tile with enemies A to up to G gets placed too. That way whenever we shuffle anything around it becomes obvious if they need to take an immediate turn, or how deadly the foe's current initiative is at. We tend to use Theatre of the Mind, so it takes the place of a combat map.<br /> <br /> Also we have two forms of morte/willpower counting for the taste of the player in question. One is an abacus with several different sections and colours that you can shuffle around for each of those pools. Another is a 4 section subdivided box, with larger coloured beads, and pools for willpower, personal, peripheral, and discarded motes. That way you also get the visceral feeling of picking up a mitt full of motes and willpower and tumbling them into the &quot;Spent&quot; box before pulling off your epic move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:49:16-08:00","id":1285160,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately my experiences have been pretty close to those of Gonzo and Croakamancer, at least for how the system works. I've had fun playing (well, mostly running) 3E, sure, but I've had more fun running the Exalted setting using non-Exalted systems lately.<br /> <br /> Pros:<br /> <br /> 1. The intent of cinematic combat with the withering/decisive is quite interesting.<br /> 2. A lot of the side systems are good in concept, if not always in execution. Investigation, sorcery and sorcerous workings, and many of the social influence systems are both interesting and seem to work well in play. Others, like craft, are at least interesting ideas.<br /> 3. Exalted continues to have one of my favorite settings, and I do love a lot of the locations and ideas added in 3E.<br /> 4. Some fixes from 2E. More or less removing perfects was probably a good call, for example.<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> <br /> 1. Far too little official material. I don't have time to write my own Evocation trees, try to get together the still missing splats that are pretty central to the Exalted setting, or other in depth rewrites that I might have been inclined to do when I was a younger person with more free time. As a GM, that means I'm limited to a very narrow range of options when it comes to opposing a group of Solar level characters, and I don't have a huge inclination to put down $2 per NPC sheet sight unseen either. 3E has been available for sale for almost three years and has exactly two published books. I'd need at least a new collection of sample non-Solar Exalts to ever consider running 3E again.<br /> 2. Many of the Pro category up above seem like good ideas, but it's hard to agree on which ones work out in execution as well as they look on paper. I've had several groups say that the withering/decisive thing still wasn't working out for them after 3-4 sessions, which seems to not really jive with the overall community experience here, so I don't know what we were doing differently. Likewise, I know I will never touch the as-written craft system ever again, but I also know there are people here who love it. I'm not sure why they even wasted the wordcount on the leadership &quot;system&quot;, since it basically boils down to &quot;figure it out yourself&quot; spaced out over three pages.<br /> 3. Reconciling setting information for three editions of Exalted across multiple writing teams is getting harder and harder, which is problematic for a group that has some players who go back to 1E and some who are jumping on at 3E. My idea of how the Realm &quot;works&quot; probably isn't the same as yours at this point, unless you're one of three other people who happened to be sitting around the same gaming tables I've been at over the better parts of two decades.<br /> 4. Charm bloat. Many Solar Charms are very boring if you're not into number crunching, and even enthusiastic min-maxers I've played with have indicated there are probably too many either way. Not going to talk about this one much, as it seems to be one of the common &quot;cons&quot; in the other lists.<br /> 5. Some of the mechanics could be laid out in a more concise, precise manner.<br /> 6. The retention of the difference in Bonus Points at creation and Experience during play. As things stand now, it's really hard for me to not look at character creation as a &quot;winnable&quot; (or more importantly, &quot;loseable&quot;) minigame, a state of affairs which I loathe.<br /> 7. I dislike much of the core book art, at least compared to 2E's core. Though not as bad as the backer draft, I still find many pieces of the art from the 3E core pretty bad, and really dislike the cover. I probably wouldn't buy it in a store if I had leafed through it first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T02:42:08-08:00","id":1285174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285084#post1285084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Exalted comes even remotely close to pretending the characters are anything but god-kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I can see what the posters getting at. At one level you are a starting hero yet also a demigod. But we aren\u2019t presented with many premade oppositions that aren\u2019t scrubs or other Exalts or Multiple Tyrant Lizards.<br /> <br /> Like honestly you shouldn\u2019t be fighting just one god. If you are a circle of Solars you need to be fighting multiple spirits, bolster by mortal human or beast mooks. Otberwise it\u2019s the early storyarch of those Animes/Mangas were the main Character is obviously outclassing everyone like One Punch Man or Luffy. A single God and Some Bandits are probably not going to be a threat to a whole Circle of Exalts, much less Solars. It may be a threat to a single solar though.<br /> <br /> There is some dissonance, well until we get more books. Where at the same time your a starting video game hero... except you are also Boss villain level slugger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:15:01-08:00","id":1285225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285086#post1285086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you want to use them for?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're fine until you hit the part where your character needs a character sheet for his alternate motivations to work. Then you start having to make other character sheets with their own abilities and charms. I tried making a character with almost all the persona charms at start and the other character sheets were pretty worthless and very much a waste of XP. This is the one case where I would have been fine with them stealing from sidereals (as opposed to the other times when I was mad about it) and just had alternate persona's have minor abilities similar to resplendencies that let you fake being competent at something you might not be rather than forcing you to make multiple character sheets most of which are almost entirely worthless and a shitload time to make the character work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-06-2019, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:17:52-08:00","id":1285227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285084#post1285084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Exalted comes even remotely close to pretending the characters are anything but god-kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It pretends that the solars are underdogs but I guess in sense that it's 300 versus hundreds of thousands, sure. In the sense that they constantly have to struggle well, on paper sure in practice the opponents solars are given when they are allowed to have their best charms up front is just a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:19:20-08:00","id":1285230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285143#post1285143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should also mention that our group had major problems with this as well until we came up with physical solutions, so that should factor into my pro/cons. A particularly crafty member of our group, like in real life, build a little board with moveable tiles and a big double-wide number line for initiative. Now whenever we go into combat a tile with each of our names on it goes onto the board and a tile with enemies A to up to G gets placed too. That way whenever we shuffle anything around it becomes obvious if they need to take an immediate turn, or how deadly the foe's current initiative is at. We tend to use Theatre of the Mind, so it takes the place of a combat map.</div> </div> </div> </div>My group did something similar, albeit less crafty, where we used a dry-erase map (Paizo's Flip Mat, if you are interested) and then numbered it and dropped miniatures on the map as representative for each player and enemy. Using that, it really wasn't bad at all to track initiative and it does provide, at a glance, who is at dangerous levels of initiative and controlling the fight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T07:19:16-08:00","id":1285239,"title":"","content":"I play over Skype, so on my computer. Thus, I write initiative, motes and wp on a word doc or notepad and just edit as I go. So it's fairly easy to keep track, though I somethimes forget to regen motes (but that's easy enough to put in later,ie if I forget for 3 rounds, then I can add 15.<br /> <br /> When I ran the game though, I often lost track of whose go it was. I found the best thing was to get them to track it themselves, and read out a count-down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T08:34:49-08:00","id":1285251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285227#post1285227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It pretends that the solars are underdogs but I guess in sense that it's 300 versus hundreds of thousands, sure. In the sense that they constantly have to struggle well, on paper sure in practice the opponents solars are given when they are allowed to have their best charms up front is just a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's supposed to be Luke Skywalker vs the Empire; they're outnumbered, but obviously Luke can take on 10 stormtroopers and win.<br /> <br /> In theory, the Realm is still a huge threat because they have 70 Dragonblood and 4000 soldiers per Solar, but obviously it's not practical for me to run a fight between 6 Solars and 420 Dragonblood. So it ends up being 6 Solars vs 6 Dragonblood, and unsurprisingly, the Solars wipe the floor with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T08:40:01-08:00","id":1285253,"title":"","content":"(I kind of want to run a Size 2 unit of 30 Might 3 elite-drill Dragonblooded led by an Essence 5 general, and 2-3 other Essence 4 DBs, but everyone tells me you can't put Dragonblood in battle groups. But how else do you run 30 Dragonblood attacking the PCs?<br /> This comes back, to some extent, to the lack of foes for high-level Solars.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-06-2019, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T08:54:04-08:00","id":1285258,"title":"","content":"Pros:<br /> The Social system has got to be the best in any RPG, bar none. <br /> Creation is one of the few settings that I actually want to run. I usually homebrew.<br /> The combat is very very interesting.<br /> Charms make me excited to build characters, and I think that's pretty high praise.<br /> Mechanically I think most of the game is extremely well executed. <br /> I think it's worth reiterating that I love the new take on the setting. The reduction is &quot;science fiction pretending to be fantasy&quot; was a really wise move, I think. The Realm is awesome now. I'm really excited to see a version of Lunars that's not thoroughly bad. <br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> While I don't have the visceral hatred of craft that some do and have seen it work out great in play, it takes a lot of work to get it working properly.<br /> It's an intimidating system. While I really like that, I have a group that's too scared to give it a try. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284810#post1284810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#2: Every single setting change, bar 'remove obviously gross thing', was for the worse. Yes, <i>all of them.</i> I only put this on the list because, while it's subjective, the fact that the setting is so different from the way I like it makes it really annoying to ST: it's hard to lay down changed fluff to players who're jumping on board now and don't have the older books.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is somewhat amazing to me. Not at all a personal attack, but I can't imagine reading through WFHW and thinking, &quot;Man, I wish Dragonblooded sucked on a thematic and ontological level again!&quot; Every Great House description made me want to run a different campaign. Ex3 has been pretty polarizing in a lot of ways, I guess. (Again, I'm not trying to be antagonistic, I think it's worth discussing differences of opinion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T09:41:06-08:00","id":1285267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285258#post1285258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is somewhat amazing to me. Not at all a personal attack, but I can't imagine reading through WFHW and thinking, &quot;Man, I wish Dragonblooded sucked on a thematic and ontological level again!&quot; Every Great House description made me want to run a different campaign. Ex3 has been pretty polarizing in a lot of ways, I guess. (Again, I'm not trying to be antagonistic, I think it's worth discussing differences of opinion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>For 'not trying to be antagonistic' and 'not a personal attack' describing my prefered take as 'sucking on a thematic and ontological level' is... a <i>unique </i>approach. :P<br /> <br /> People want different things out of this setting. For me, the science fiction aspects were a great and memorable part of Exalted, and it's the lesser for trying to obfuscate them. I also really enjoyed 2E Lunars and their Silver Pact, and while new rules will be great, I await the fluff take with dread. (Yeah, I don't have to use it but as a ST I have to beat it out of the heads of new players why I want a different take at my table). I like the concept of the Thousand Dooms and continue to view Solars vs the Realm as the least interesting story you can tell in the setting.<br /> <br /> Really, I think this is the retrospect on 3E. It's still divisive. The arguments died down somewhat with the new dev team but our perspectives on the edition are still really diverse. WFHW hasn't changed that. It'll be interesting to see if Lunars does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T09:48:26-08:00","id":1285270,"title":"","content":"*Nothing to see here really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 02-06-2019, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:04:25-08:00","id":1285274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285270#post1285270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may be walking on thin ice here but... those things don't need a new edition to go away, you simply change them in your game and voila. I understand, and don't mean to say you're wrong. In fact, you know better than anyone what you prefer and need.<br /> <br /> I remember a time in which loooong arguments were made on this forum about the oversexualization in certain illustrations and some setting content. <br /> <br /> Ex3 is almost completly deprived of those things... and I might be the only one in this corner, but I think some part of the games identity has died in the process... it's like Exalted has been tamed, and it used to be wild and brave. Meh... <br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I do not support evil and/or evil actions in any way or form, please know to differentiate my humble point of view from any kind of apology for evil behaviors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. That material is stuff that did not enhance the setting. I do not miss it. I almost agree with you, the sense of Exalted as bold or intriguing has faded, but I don't think it's down to us having a basic sense of taste here. There's no real 'baby with the bathwater' omission from the mature content cuts, IMO at least","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:07:09-08:00","id":1285277,"title":"","content":"I like warstriders very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 02-06-2019, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:07:28-08:00","id":1285278,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar90_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"90\" data-vbnamecard=\"90\">Gonzo</a>: Please don't say you don't support evil in the same breath as you lionize material that makes light of rape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:17:46-08:00","id":1285280,"title":"","content":"Let's all ignore my last posts. There's no need to turn this into anything else. I'll delete them, but if a mod can come and destroy them I'd be grateful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:31:19-08:00","id":1285288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285251#post1285251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it's supposed to be Luke Skywalker vs the Empire; they're outnumbered, but obviously Luke can take on 10 stormtroopers and win.<br /> <br /> In theory, the Realm is still a huge threat because they have 70 Dragonblood and 4000 soldiers per Solar, but obviously it's not practical for me to run a fight between 6 Solars and 420 Dragonblood. So it ends up being 6 Solars vs 6 Dragonblood, and unsurprisingly, the Solars wipe the floor with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but it took a while for luke to do that. I feel that building up to power is mpre enjoyable than just having a murder combo at start. At beast imo supernal should have just counted you one or two essense higher rather than just 5 at start. Though i understand that it depends on the game and that not every game will last long enough to enjoy those high level techniques. I feel like it takes away more than it adds.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, on the subject on new versus old i'm a fan of mixing and matching but i definitely prefer the 1e dragon blooded setting than the 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-06-2019, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:04:22-08:00","id":1285300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285253#post1285253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I kind of want to run a Size 2 unit of 30 Might 2 elite-drill Dragonblooded led by an Essence 5 general, and 2-3 other Essence 4 DBs, but everyone tells me you can't put Dragonblood in battle groups. But how else do you run 30 Dragonblood attacking the PCs?<br /> This comes back, to some extent, to the lack of foes for high-level Solars.)</div> </div> </div> </div>*checks book*<br /> <br /> Might 3 surely? I would also be interested to see how that would hash out. True you'd have the PCs dropping exalts like flies whenever they attacked, but if we assume artifact armour and weapons, and with a total of +5 to attack and damage, a flat +4 to their defence and a big AoE attack that could be pretty deadly. If we make the assumption of 3 in every stat that's still like a base parry of 9, attack with base 10, damage of 18, and soak of 13. <br /> <br /> Then if the General is essence 4-5 you use Blessed Dragon Champion combined with Wildfire Legion, combo' with Blazing Courageous Swordsman Inspiration and max out Tactics Mean Everything. Then you stunt and spend a willpower on the command roll, then stunt and spend a willpower on the attack...actually that might be going too far. If the attack was only targeting the dawn of the party then it'd probably be okay, but that's likely to crash everyone who's not really powerful on defence. And if you're crashed then the battlegroup does almost that same attack again next turn but kills you, hope you disengaged. Even worse if somebody does get incapacitated it resets Wildfire Legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:06:59-08:00","id":1285303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285267#post1285267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have to use it but as a ST I have to beat it out of the heads of new players why I want a different take at my table</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds kind of Draconian as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Personal tastes aside, that just doesn't sound like good conduct as a Storyteller. Seems like the kind of thing one ought to move past for the sake of one's players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:19:38-08:00","id":1285307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285303#post1285303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds kind of Draconian as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Personal tastes aside, that just doesn't sound like good conduct as a Storyteller. Seems like the kind of thing one ought to move past for the sake of one's players.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not fair to the st who wants to run something but can't because of &quot;canon&quot;. It's there for setting cohesion but you shouldn't be beholden to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:23:52-08:00","id":1285313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285300#post1285300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *checks book*<br /> <br /> Might 3 surely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but if we assume artifact armour and weapons, and with a total of +5 to attack and damage, a flat +4 to their defence and a big AoE attack that could be pretty deadly. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't actually, I'd probably put all the non-BG Dragonblood in artefact armour and weapons, but not the Battle Group. Because when they die, I wouldn't want the PCs to find 30 suits of artefact armour and 30 daiklaives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we make the assumption of 3 in every stat that's still like a base parry of 9, attack with base 10, damage of 18, and soak of 13. </div> </div> </div>Nah, use Elite Soldier stats. That seems fair for an Essence 1-2, non-min-maxed Dragonblood officer. (Also I'm lazy.)<br /> So it looks like this: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">10</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">16 (Dmg 17, min 2)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">9</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">9</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">12</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">9</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">4</td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> .actually that might be going too far. If the attack was only targeting the dawn of the party then it'd probably be okay, but that's likely to crash everyone who's not really powerful on defence. And if you're crashed then the battlegroup does almost that same attack again next turn but kills you, hope you disengaged. Even worse if somebody does get incapacitated it resets Wildfire Legion. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the point. Being attacked by 30 Dragonblood <i>should</i> be terrifying, even for the PCs in the game I ran (5 Essence 5 Solars, 2 Essence 5 Lunars).<br /> It may seem ridiculous, but they're essence 5 Solars, they'll bust out their own ridiculous stuff. Ridiculous defences, counterattacks, etc.<br /> (Except the social character, but she'd be a range band or two back because she's not an idiot.)<br /> <br /> The thing is, it can do a lot of damage, but as you say, they'll drop like flies, they've only got 17 health levels between them (though Defence 9 and Soak 12 isn't to be sniffed at). It's a glass cannon, essentially.<br /> (Which does mean you can run the combat at good speed, but it makes it swingy.)<br /> <br /> The most important charm for the DB commander is actually Enfolded in the Dragon's Wings to buff their defence and soak, and keep them alive through a couple of rounds of being attacked by 5 Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:27:03-08:00","id":1285315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285288#post1285288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but it took a while for luke to do that. I feel that building up to power is mpre enjoyable than just having a murder combo at start. At beast imo supernal should have just counted you one or two essense higher rather than just 5 at start. Though i understand that it depends on the game and that not every game will last long enough to enjoy those high level techniques. I feel like it takes away more than it adds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do somewhat agree with you, but I actually feel Supernal is less an issue than all those 5s.<br /> <br /> When I made a starting character, I found I actually only bought Essence 2 charms, because of prereqs and wanting to buy charms from other Abilities.<br /> <br /> So... I guess I wouldn't mind if it was just like +2 Essence. I suppose I can see that some idiot might buy 15 Melee charms, make combat unfun, and find there's nowhere for them go Melee-wise.<br /> <br /> But it's not an issue I've actually seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:30:44-08:00","id":1285317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285315#post1285315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do somewhat agree with you, but I actually feel Supernal is less an issue than all those 5s.<br /> <br /> When I made a starting character, I found I actually only bought Essence 2 charms, because of prereqs and wanting to buy charms from other Abilities.<br /> <br /> So... I guess I wouldn't mind if it was just like +2 Essence. I suppose I can see that some idiot might buy 15 Melee charms, make combat unfun, and find there's nowhere for them go Melee-wise.<br /> <br /> But it's not an issue I've actually seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really because that was one I've seen. Some trees aren't good before E3 and the interesting charm tress require sufficient investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:36:04-08:00","id":1285319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285313#post1285313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's the point. Being attacked by 30 Dragonblood <i>should</i> be terrifying, even for the PCs in the game I ran (5 Essence 5 Solars, 2 Essence 5 Lunars).<br /> It may seem ridiculous, but they're essence 5 Solars, they'll bust out their own ridiculous stuff. Ridiculous defences, counterattacks, etc.<br /> (Except the social character, but she'd be a range band or two back because she's not an idiot.)<br /> <br /> The most important charm for the DB commander is actually Enfolded in the Dragon's Wings to buff their defence and soak, and keep them alive through a couple of rounds of being attacked by 5 Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow, seven essence 5 celestial exalts? I do not envy you. Also I doubt even that crazy group would do much. I was thinking about what if you unleashed it on a group of 4-5 essence 2 or 3 Solars. In your case I doubt it would do much. One of the easy ways to almost totally nullify the battlegroup is o just beat the initiative roll of the dragonblooded commander, and launch a series of decisive attacks on it like with melee or especially brawl. The soak won't matter, you get a ton of free damage for attacking with a decisive, and Enfolded only braces against one attack. It's something you would have trouble doing at chargen not just because you don't have the motes, but at essence 5 it's easy, you can even use any leftover attacks to beat up the other DBs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285315#post1285315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not an issue I've actually seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, not only have I seen that issue multiple times, I've done it myself by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-06-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:38:21-08:00","id":1285321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285303#post1285303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds kind of Draconian as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Personal tastes aside, that just doesn't sound like good conduct as a Storyteller. Seems like the kind of thing one ought to move past for the sake of one's players.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285307#post1285307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not fair to the st who wants to run something but can't because of &quot;canon&quot;. It's there for setting cohesion but you shouldn't be beholden to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite. &quot;My table, my take&quot; is hardly draconian, it's a baseline of RPG play and the DM/Player relationship. Do you think I should feel obliged to ST stories with a version of the setting I dislike just because it's what's in the newest book? Forcing players to read a massive additional setting bible or getting mad about slip ups would be draconian, but asking players to abide by my preferences as a ST is just reasonable boundary setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T12:08:20-08:00","id":1285329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285160#post1285160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Far too little official material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did find this to be a big issue when the game came out. Especially as my game was a continuation of a 2nd ed game, so they were at Essence 4 (I argued that Essence 4 was the new 5, to knock them down, but I didn't think I could get away with cutting them down even more), making the antagonist in the back of the book even more useless.<br /> The only ones I got any real use out of were Elite Soldiers (for Battle Groups) and Ahlat.<br /> <br /> I think it's a lot better now, though I'd still like more powerful stuff. There's some good powerful stuff in Hundred Devils (like the lava-behemoth, I'd really like to see our ST use that, he said he would but so far hasn't) but not enough, and none of the Antagonists of the Righteous are very powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a huge inclination to put down $2 per NPC sheet sight unseen either.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you click on &quot;Full-Size Preview&quot; you can see the first page or two. That generally gives me enough information to know whether I want to buy it or not (not always, because I can't see anything about the second Hundred Devils entry, but generally).<br /> <br /> I think it'd help if the description actually said what they were, rather than being a generic description, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3E has been available for sale for almost three years and has exactly two published books. </div> </div> </div>I suppose this is kind of true.* You can get Dragonblood on BackerKit though.<br /> <br /> *Though technically it's the Core, Miracles and Arms.<br /> <br /> I think that it's going to speed up now, Vance and Minton seem to be going at a decent rate, but the big gap between the kickstart of the Core and its release, and then between its release and the release of Arms, makes it look pretty bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd need at least a new collection of sample non-Solar Exalts to ever consider running 3E again. </div> </div> </div>That's what Adversaries of the Righteous basically is, but it's very slow.*<br /> <br /> *Partly because it's slowed to one character a month, but also because sometimes they do mortals, which are a waste of time IMO because I don't need stats for mortals, I can do that myself in 30 seconds. Or even as they need them.<br /> But the two Dragonblood, Exigent, Sidereal, Lunar, Raksha and god they've done are all decent (well, the Exigent is a bit weak, but I liked her).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've had several groups say that the withering/decisive thing still wasn't working out for them after 3-4 sessions, which seems to not really jive with the overall community experience here, so I don't know what we were doing differently. </div> </div> </div>For us, I'd say that 3-4 sessions was about the time it took to grok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure why they even wasted the wordcount on the leadership &quot;system&quot;, since it basically boils down to &quot;figure it out yourself&quot; spaced out over three pages. </div> </div> </div>People seem to expect it. I've seen people say it's good, and others that they want it to involve even more stuff.<br /> Personally I skimmed it. I don't see any need for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. The retention of the difference in Bonus Points at creation and Experience during play. As things stand now, it's really hard for me to not look at character creation as a &quot;winnable&quot; (or more importantly, &quot;loseable&quot;) minigame, a state of affairs which I loathe. </div> </div> </div>You've expressed my thoughts pretty much exactly.<br /> <br /> Exalted's character gen system is fast (except for deciding on your 15 charms, of course), and straightforward. But it is, as you say, a loseable minigame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. I dislike much of the core book art, at least compared to 2E's core. Though not as bad as the backer draft, I still find many pieces of the art from the 3E core pretty bad, and really dislike the cover. I probably wouldn't buy it in a store if I had leafed through it first. </div> </div> </div>I recently went back and looked at my copy of the 2nd ed Core, and yeah, it's way better. It comes off as having a more uniform style, and the Ameri-manga style of much of it immediately tells you what the game is about.<br /> (1st ed's Core had some absolutely awful art in though. A few nice pieces, but a lot of trash.)<br /> <br /> There are pieces I like in the 3rd ed Core, but 2nd ed does have much better quality art.<br /> <br /> (Though we've laughed for years at that picture of a Zenith killing a dog in the combat rules.)<br /> <br /> Miracles has really good art though, and Arms and Dragonblood are pretty good. There's a particular artist they used a fair bit in Arms and Dragonblood that I really like (I don't know their name though).<br /> <br /> <br /> Art, the clarity of the mechanics, how bloated the charmset is, how slow books come out, the small amount of antagonists written up...<br /> These are all problems that have, frankly, got much better since the Core book came out (unsurprisingly for the first one).<br /> I'd say the only thing I'd hoped would improve that hasn't is the amount of tracking that needs to be done (since Dragonblood have to keep track of their Aura, which is itself a bit fiddly). Though I don't see that Lunars are going to have stuff to keep track of that Solars don't.<br /> <br /> And, while there are bits that maybe aren't great in the core mechanics of the game, overall I think it is good (though I can see parts are still contraversial). It's certainly way more balanced than 2nd ed. Despite the good art and writing of some of the 2nd ed books (though not all!), the base system was problematic, meaning it needed to be errata'd in big ways.<br /> I don't think that's necessary with 3rd ed's combat system and social system.<br /> <br /> And this is why I'm really looking forward to Lunars. I'm hoping, maybe next year or something, I can run a Lunars game where the antagonists are Dragonblood, sorcerers, demons, monsters, and the odd other Exalt, and so if there are problems with the Solar charmset it doesn't matter much.<br /> (And if some people really, really want to play Solars, they'll likely be people who like the Solar charmset rather than those who don't.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-06-2019, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T12:47:14-08:00","id":1285339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285267#post1285267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For 'not trying to be antagonistic' and 'not a personal attack' describing my prefered take as 'sucking on a thematic and ontological level' is... a <i>unique </i>approach. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I included so many disclaimers! I was trying to make clear that I don't think your take sucks--it's just my reading of <i>2e's canon</i> that <i>Dragonblooded</i> suck. Their inferiority seems to be hammered in again and again, in big and small ways. Compare that to Ex3, where they're presented more as the heroes of their own stories. <br /> <br /> So to more explicitly state why I brought it up and quoted you, I guess I'd like to know either a) why you prefer the 'suckier' DBs of 2e, or b) why you think my priors are incorrect and 2e's DBs aren't suckier at all! (Or any third option, if how we're thinking about DBs in Exalted is completely orthogonal.)<br /> <br /> All my disclaimers are because I'm genuinely interested in your opinion, and I'm trying to make it very clear that I'm not sealioning you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:03:44-08:00","id":1285345,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tried the naval system?<br /> <br /> Like... that's a new system. It doesn't look very complex. There are charms that are based on it. And my ST was probably going to use it when the Realm invades the land of lakes we're just south of.<br /> <br /> But I've never seen it used, so I don't know how it is in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:11:29-08:00","id":1285346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285345#post1285345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tried the naval system?</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather enjoyed it in my West game. Haven't tried it with Spider or Knight Raiton, though Carter Brus <i>does</i> have dots in Sail, now that you mention it\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:12:59-08:00","id":1285347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285339#post1285339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I included so many disclaimers! I was trying to make clear that I don't think your take sucks--it's just my reading of <i>2e's canon</i> that <i>Dragonblooded</i> suck. Their inferiority seems to be hammered in again and again, in big and small ways. Compare that to Ex3, where they're presented more as the heroes of their own stories.<br /> <br /> So to more explicitly state why I brought it up and quoted you, I guess I'd like to know either a) why you prefer the 'suckier' DBs of 2e, or b) why you think my priors are incorrect and 2e's DBs aren't suckier at all! (Or any third option, if how we're thinking about DBs in Exalted is completely orthogonal.)<br /> <br /> All my disclaimers are because I'm genuinely interested in your opinion, and I'm trying to make it very clear that I'm not sealioning you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With you, and not mad..<br /> <br /> *hums* Honestly, the text you're talking about is something less direct and clear cut. There's no one para in 2E that flat out says 'Dragonblooded are Lame and Solars are Awesome'. What's generally brought up are those passages from the Manual of Exalted Power that get derogatory about the role the Dragon Blooded had in the First Age. And that never bothered me. Whatever they might have been created to be like, the Dragon Blooded today are the Princes of the Earth, and had centuries to grow into that role. All that stuff about their origins is prologue: the Dragons of the present day were cool to me. If the mechanics didn't back that up, that sucks but just in fluff terms they felt like they <i>ought </i>to be cool. The Vegeta to a Solar Goku if you will.<br /> <br /> Now, the fact that the setting tends to take pot shots at Dragon Blooded rule and loves to go on and on about how awesome our shiny overlords are and how they made things all better and people just all loved them... yeah, <i>that </i>grated on me. I'd like more respect given to the Dragon Blooded. I'd like the Shogunate to be a cool time period that could mean something to players, even if it was far from perfect. I'd like to be able to talk up the Realm as this morally complex thing, an oppressive homogenizing empire that is still capable of doing good, driving back the Fae, defending Creation from actual threats.<br /> <br /> Tarnished bronze. Lesser, corrupted and in need of improvement, but safe.<br /> <br /> Buuuut I don't feel that 3E tackles those complaints. If anything dev commentary seems to suggest the intent is to lean further into the stuff I dislike: that trying to make an oppressive empire morally complex is the same thing as excusing Imperialism. *sigh* That's for a different thread, this is just me outlining my PoV on the edition changes since you asked. (I also kinda think WFHW leaned a little into Flanderization of the Great Houses... but just a little, and some of the new ideas I did like. Kinda evens on that front.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:16:23-08:00","id":1285348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285346#post1285346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather enjoyed it in my West game. Haven't tried it with Spider or Knight Raiton, though Carter Brus <i>does</i> have dots in Sail, now that you mention it\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>This was with Captain... Barbus? Barbar? I can't remember their name exactly.<br /> <br /> I guess a Western game used it a lot.<br /> <br /> What did you like about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:16:51-08:00","id":1285350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285347#post1285347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hehe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With you, and not mad..<br /> <br /> *hums* Honestly, the text you're talking about is something less direct and clear cut. There's no one para in 2E that flat out says 'Dragonblooded are Lame and Solars are Awesome'.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they put that in sidereals and Yu-shan. However, I feel you should try 1st edition dragon blooded because it was a better written book and is much more favorable to dragon blooded than 2e was. Most of 2e was just a copy and paste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-06-2019, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:23:16-08:00","id":1285355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285350#post1285350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they put that in sidereals and Yu-shan. However, I feel you should try 1st edition because it was a better written book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the 'gods hate Dragon Blooded because they're not the rightful Princes of the Earth' thing?<br /> <br /> That's BS but that's a sidebar, and IIRC rooted in 1E (at least one of the Aspect books made a thing of Shogunate Dragons not being able to win deities respect for the same reason), Never felt like a core component of their portrayal, and when it came up felt more that it meant the gods were stupid jerks rather than DBs sucked at all. There was also that bit in the Daystar write up about how there was this sacred super sword meant for the leader of the Exalted host and no Dragon Blood could <i>hope </i>to gain permission to wield it.<br /> <br /> To this day, as a Dragon Blooded fan, I take that as a challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (As to 1E... well I've probably been biased against it by all the 3E fans telling me that 1E is superior in just about every way to 2E. I've read a fair amount of it and seldom find that to stack up personally. Did you have a specific book in mind?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:25:43-08:00","id":1285357,"title":"","content":"Edit: Ninja'd<br /> <br /> Yeah, 1st ed had a lot of cultural details that were a bit missing from 2nd ed. Though I still thought 2nd ed Dragonblood was a good book (except for the charm writer's inability to understand Steps and poor ability to balance charms against each other).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also kinda think WFHW leaned a little into Flanderization of the Great Houses... but just a little, and some of the new ideas I did like. Kinda evens on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expected to hate all the new stuff, because I did like the old Houses, but yeah, some of the new ideas actually ended up being quite good.<br /> <br /> As for flanderisation... yeah, I can see that, but it's not nearly as bad as I thought it'd be when Morke originally was talking about it. I don't know if that's because he was focusing on changes, trying to convince people who didn't like the old houses that the new ones were different, or because it ended up written by someone else, but either way, I was happy with the result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like the Shogunate to be a cool time period that could mean something to players, even if it was far from perfect. </div> </div> </div>I'd like it to be cool, but most of all I'd just like PCs to have learned more than 2 paragraphs about it in school. Even if it's not that interesting, I'd like Dragonblood to know what their own history is. And that needs players to know about it, rather than knowing a ton of ancient Solar pre-history and very little about the Dragonblood's own golden age (which would likely have better preserved records).<br /> <br /> The new Dragonblood is, I have to say, better in terms of presenting history than the old book, though we'll see how things are in the Realm book.<br /> <br /> As to presentation of the Empire, I didn't actually find the Dragonblood book to be painting everyone in the Realm as pure evil. It may just be something that was said on forums. But on the other hand, that'd be more in the Realm book than What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:32:26-08:00","id":1285360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285355#post1285355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the 'gods hate Dragon Blooded because they're not the rightful Princes of the Earth' thing?<br /> <br /> That's BS but that's a sidebar, and IIRC rooted in 1E (at least one of the Aspect books made a thing of Shogunate Dragons not being able to win deities respect for the same reason), Never felt like a core component of their portrayal, and when it came up felt more that it meant the gods were stupid jerks rather than DBs sucked at all. There was also that bit in the Daystar write up about how there was this sacred super sword meant for the leader of the Exalted host and no Dragon Blood could <i>hope </i>to gain permission to wield it.<br /> <br /> To this day, as a Dragon Blooded fan, I take that as a challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (As to 1E... well I've probably been biased against it by all the 3E fans telling me that 1E is superior in just about every way to 2E. I've read a fair amount of it and seldom find that to stack up personally. Did you have a specific book in mind?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think the first edition DB book is better than second edition and 3rd. Not mechanics obviously but there is a lot of attention to detail that the other two editions never bothered with. Personally, I'm very mixed on 3E but a lot of the core books were handled better in 1e. There are some things I like more in 2e but you have to realize, in the beginning of 2e was just churning out all the books as fast as possible which lead to the sidereal charmset being really poorly ported and the scroll of the monk. Like sidereals are my favorite exalt. I read both editions of that book more times than I can count and I can tell you massive chunks were wholesale lifted and what little wasn't lifted was put into yu-shan. There was a number of things that didn't get ported though, which just made 2e worse in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-06-2019, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:38:44-08:00","id":1285363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285355#post1285355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As to 1E... well I've probably been biased against it by all the 3E fans telling me that 1E is superior in just about every way to 2E. I've read a fair amount of it and seldom find that to stack up personally. Did you have a specific book in mind?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the fluff of the Aspect Books Abyssals, Blood and Salt, Cult of the Illuminated, Dragonblooded, Houses of the Bull God, Manacle and Coin and Outcastes. In some cases (Abyssals, Outcastes) more than the 2nd ed equivalent (a lot more for Lookshy. I am not a fan of Compass: Scavenger Lands).<br /> <br /> Scavenger Sons has good and bad bits, but the scale is very bad. Savage Seas I found dull, Kingdom of Halta has terrible demographics, Lunars has a few nice bits but is mostly very one-dimensional. Ruins of Rathess comes off, to me, as a bit silly. Bastions of the North I liked one-third of, and not the other two-thirds. Time of Tumult is mixed. The Caste Books are okay but nothing special.<br /> <br /> 2nd ed Lunars and Compass: North are, I think, much better than their 1st edition equivalents. Masters of Jade is probably better than Manacle and Coin, but Manacle and Coin is still quite good. And a lot of stuff doesn't have much of an equivalent in 1st ed so isn't comparable.<br /> And some stuff is basically the same anyway.<br /> <br /> (The other stuff I don't have copies of. I hear Games of Divinity is better than its 2nd ed equivalents, but I only skimmed my friend's copy once, so I can't comment on that. It's probably hard to rate; I like the Malfeas book but not some of the other demon fluff, I don't love or hate Yu-Shan, I like Glories: Luna and Glories: Maidens but not Glories: UCS, and obviously in 1st ed they didn't have seperate books.)<br /> <br /> <br /> So it's quite mixed.<br /> 2nd ed has way better art though. I liked the comics a lot more than 1st ed/3rd ed's prose intros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-06-2019, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:39:44-08:00","id":1285364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285357#post1285357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expected to hate all the new stuff, because I did like the old Houses, but yeah, some of the new ideas actually ended up being quite good.<br /> <br /> As for flanderisation... yeah, I can see that, but it's not nearly as bad as I thought it'd be when Morke originally was talking about it. I don't know if that's because he was focusing on changes, trying to convince people who didn't like the old houses that the new ones were different, or because it ended up written by someone else, but either way, I was happy with the result.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* It's not a big deal, like... it feels like we got a clearer feel for each house as a distinct entity, their culture, how they fit into the framework of Realm society and what others think of them, but it came at the cost of making it seem like DBs of a given house had to fit into the ideas of that house, or counterconform. I don't hate the 3E take, and enjoyed reading it, just feel like it's worth taking it with a grain of salt. I might be in the process of planning a game with Dragon Blooded clones, an Albert Wesker expy and lifting the opening scene of Final Fantasy VII (only now with zombies and a Kraken), but even I have a silliness threshold. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like it to be cool, but most of all I'd just like PCs to have learned more than 2 paragraphs about it in school. Even if it's not that interesting, I'd like Dragonblood to know what their own history is. And that needs players to know about it, rather than knowing a ton of ancient Solar pre-history and very little about the Dragonblood's own golden age (which would likely have better preserved records).<br /> <br /> The new Dragonblood is, I have to say, better in terms of presenting history than the old book, though we'll see how things are in the Realm book.<br /> <br /> As to presentation of the Empire, I didn't actually find the Dragonblood book to be painting everyone in the Realm as pure evil. It may just be something that was said on forums. But on the other hand, that'd be more in the Realm book than What Fire Has Wrought. </div> </div> </div>It's mostly past forumite content at this point. I was trying to say that while I felt there was room for improvement in 2Es portrayal dev commentary (and writer commentary) suggests the team don't see the matter quite the same way I do.<br /> <br /> Eh. We agree on the need for more Shogunate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Why wasn't 'history of the Shogunate' a part of Heirs again?) I still don't think we've got much but here's hoping more's to come","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:45:26-08:00","id":1285365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285347#post1285347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for taking the time to go through all that! I don't agree with all of it, but you definitely make some good points. One of the things I'm hoping for as The Realm and Lunars come out is more of that moral complexity, especially regarding the Immaculate Philosophy where I think there's a lot of room for it. I'd contend that those themes are at least somewhat present--Ledaal is a prime example. It is complicating that the removal of the Thousand Dooms (something I like but you said you weren't crazy about) makes it harder for the Realm to be the &quot;good guys&quot; on a grand scale, just because there are much fewer threats that require a world-spanning super power to solve. I agree that there's room for moral complexity when you can frame the situation as &quot;oppressive imperial overlords vs soul-sucking aliens,&quot; but I suppose I'm more optimistic than you are that, as the setting is fleshed out, the devs will handle the Realm in an interesting way. If for no other reason than, if they don't, DBs <i>and</i> Sids look like chumps. <br /> <br /> I'm surprised to hear you describe the Great House writeups as Flanderization, because IMO most of them became more complex and in-depth. Sesus, though? I'll definitely grant you that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:50:21-08:00","id":1285367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285360#post1285360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think the first edition DB book is better than second edition and 3rd. Not mechanics obviously but there is a lot of attention to detail that the other two editions never bothered with. Personally, I'm very mixed on 3E but a lot of the core books were handled better in 1e. There are some things I like more in 2e but you have to realize, in the beginning of 2e was just churning out all the books as fast as possible which lead to the sidereal charmset being really poorly ported and the scroll of the monk. Like sidereals are my favorite exalt. I read both editions of that book more times than I can count and I can tell you massive chunks were wholesale lifted and what little wasn't lifted was put into yu-shan. There was a number of things that didn't get ported though, which just made 2e worse in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've skimmed 1e DBs. There were a few bits and pieces there, but not much that I hadn't found in other sources. <br /> <br /> And heh. I will defend 2E on many counts but mechanics are not one of them. My first reaction to hearing 3E was coming was great excitement: everyone knew 2E was a mess mechanically but we played because we loved the setting. The fact that we were not the target audience was not-fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285363#post1285363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's quite mixed.<br /> 2nd ed has way better art though. I liked the comics a lot more than 1st ed/3rd ed's prose intros.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hefty agreement on that. The comics were really trademark, something that set Ex2's books apart. The fic... does not compare. Ain't even close.<br /> <br /> It's still really interesting how much we can disagree on stuff. 2E Abyssals was my introduction to Exalted, and while its approach to 'stating' Deathlords was black comedy, a lot of its fluff I love to death. (I defend Resonance to this day as a great idea not quite well executed, but eh. Personal philosophy). Didn't really find any 1E material that wowed me or outweighed 2E. (Cult of the Illuminated was interesting matter, and probably the closest, but I prefer a slightly different take on the Gold Faction.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:51:23-08:00","id":1285368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285364#post1285364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *nods* It's not a big deal, like... it feels like we got a clearer feel for each house as a distinct entity, their culture, how they fit into the framework of Realm society and what others think of them, but it came at the cost of making it seem like DBs of a given house had to fit into the ideas of that house, or counterconform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly.<br /> <br /> I remember Morke saying he wanted to make it like Masquerade Clans, where your House is a really huge influence on you. That sounded like way too far to me.<br /> But in practice, I don't think it's so bad.<br /> <br /> I would say that it would depend on how signature examples are shown (are they all house stereotypes, or not), but most of the 3rd ed signatures aren't actually Dynasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's mostly past forumite content at this point. I was trying to say that while I felt there was room for improvement in 2Es portrayal dev commentary (and writer commentary) suggests the team don't see the matter quite the same way I do. </div> </div> </div>Sure, though I think the devs who talked a lot about it were not the ones who ended up publishing the book, since they've changed.<br /> But I don't remember exactly who said what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why wasn't 'history of the Shogunate' a part of Heirs again? </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping because it'll be in The Realm.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be a huge section. Or even accurate. What Dynasts <i>believe </i>about the Shogunate would be fine. It's just that it's quite awkward to have inter-PC conversations about it when we have no frame of reference (which I've also found to some extent with the Immaculate Philosophy, a very big part of Dynastic games, but the Devs have said they would like to do a Gods and Cults book at some point, so if the Realm doesn't cover enough of that, hopefully that will fill it in. Though it's likely years away.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:56:14-08:00","id":1285370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285367#post1285367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've skimmed 1e DBs. There were a few bits and pieces there, but not much that I hadn't found in other sources.<br /> <br /> And heh. I will defend 2E on many counts but mechanics are not one of them. My first reaction to hearing 3E was coming was great excitement: everyone knew 2E was a mess mechanically but we played because we loved the setting. The fact that we were not the target audience was not-fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think 1e presented the game much better in a neutral tone there are a lot of things I don't like about 3E and the removal of the neutral tone and feeling like there are inherent biases by the authors is one of them. 2E had that issue as well but the tone between 2E and 3E have been very different.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:58:06-08:00","id":1285371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285368#post1285368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though it's likely years away.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my problem because the last time I saw the books about to be out next sidereals wasn't even on there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:58:58-08:00","id":1285373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285365#post1285365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially regarding the Immaculate Philosophy where I think there's a lot of room for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what Vance said about the Immaculate Philosophy:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am interested in the Immaculate Faith because of its seemingly self-contradictory nature. It's a self-serving myth of Dragon-Blooded supremacy fabricated by the secret masters of the world. It's also a religion, practiced devoutly and sincerity by adherents of all stripes, that safeguards the ordinary people of Creation from the caprices of corrupt gods, provides the spiritual comfort and support of religious community, and effectively advocates on behalf of the peasantry to the Dragon-Blooded. The tension between these two truths is a powerful driver of stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is complicating that the removal of the Thousand Dooms (something I like but you said you weren't crazy about) makes it harder for the Realm to be the &quot;good guys&quot; on a grand scale, just because there are much fewer threats that require a world-spanning super power to solve. </div> </div> </div>Now they can actually succeed at defeating, say, the Deathlords, though. In 2nd ed that wasn't plausible if you used the rules as-written.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T14:01:51-08:00","id":1285375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285370#post1285370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 1e presented the game much better in a neutral tone there are a lot of things I don't like about 3E and the removal of the neutral tone and feeling like there are inherent biases by the authors is one of them. 2E had that issue as well but the tone between 2E and 3E have been very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get a biased tone from Minton or Vance. Morke had a few very strong opinions (on Solars, mostly) that I disagreed with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T14:04:58-08:00","id":1285378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285367#post1285367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals was my introduction to Exalted, and while its approach to 'stating' Deathlords was black comedy, a lot of its fluff I love to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played 2nd ed, not 1st, and so I read the 2nd ed Abyssals first. And I thought it was fine, fluff-wise.<br /> <br /> But later, when I read 1st ed Abyssals, I found I liked the 1st ed depictions of Eye and Seven Despairs, Mask of Winters, Walker in Darkness and the First and Forsaken Lion more than the 2nd ed versions.<br /> <br /> (Tbh, I don't actually remember the rest of the 1st ed Abyssals fluff, and whether it was different to 2nd ed or not. Those Deathlords are the only bits I remember.)<br /> <br /> It's not something I have such a strong opinion about than, say, the depiction of Lookshy in Outcastes vs Scavenger Lands though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T14:06:19-08:00","id":1285379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285375#post1285375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really get a biased tone from Minton or Vance. Morke had a few very strong opinions (on Solars, mostly) that I disagreed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant that the books have a tone that is inherently biased. WFHW has a clear bias in it's writing. 1e just presented it matter a factly. It wasn't dry but it didn't try to slant things one way or another. The other editions have a clear slant to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T14:07:22-08:00","id":1285381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285371#post1285371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my problem because the last time I saw the books about to be out next sidereals wasn't even on there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is now.<br /> The splatbooks are going to be Dragonblood (which I always think is out, but technically isn't), Lunars, Exigents, Sidereals. The rest aren't on there though.<br /> <br /> Non-splatbooks I think it's just Across the Eight Directions which is listed so far, and I don't know where that comes in relation to the splatbooks. It's probably not exactly on the same development cycle, as it doesn't have to be playtested or (I assume) Kickstarted.<br /> <br /> Or is the Storyteller Companion listed? I know they're keen on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T14:08:12-08:00","id":1285382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285379#post1285379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WFHW has a clear bias in it's writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T14:16:02-08:00","id":1285386,"title":"","content":"The main thing I remember about presenting stuff in 1st vs 2nd wasn't that 2nd was biased and 1st was matter-of-fact, but that the 1st ed Core book gave you two views of history; the Solar one and the orthodox Immaculate one.<br /> Which was really useful, and very lacking from 2nd ed.<br /> 2nd ed, IMO, seemed to have too much facts and not enough what people in the setting believed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T15:03:52-08:00","id":1285405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285347#post1285347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tarnished bronze. Lesser, corrupted and in need of improvement, but safe.<br /> <br /> Buuuut I don't feel that 3E tackles those complaints. If anything dev commentary seems to suggest the intent is to lean further into the stuff I dislike: that trying to make an oppressive empire morally complex is the same thing as excusing Imperialism. *sigh* That's for a different thread, this is just me outlining my PoV on the edition changes since you asked. (I also kinda think WFHW leaned a little into Flanderization of the Great Houses... but just a little, and some of the new ideas I did like. Kinda evens on that front.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my feeling on this is that I'm OK with the books being somewhat condemnatory of the Realm, so long as the substance is &quot;smart&quot;.<br /> <br /> Explaining further: On the one hand, the Realm really is meant to be an empire with specifically a pretty awful ideology - Immaculate Philosophy preaching Dragonblooded moral supremacy and the Scarlet Empress's divide and rule controlled chaos and managed low intensity internal conflict - and empires themselves are a pretty imperfect form of political organisation. There's a limit to how defensible that is. So I'm OK with the books condemning it a fair bit.<br /> <br /> On the other, I want them to describe the Realm in a way that make economic sense, and doesn't give imply weird, wrong ideas about history. No &quot;<i>Material extraction is the only reason empires happen; no ideological, military or defensive reasons. If the Realm is somewhere, they're 'On The Rob'</i>&quot;. No &quot;<i>In general, implausibly high, economically impossible levels of wealth are typically extracted under empires, keeping parts of empires that aren't the core at vastly different, vastly lower, wealth levels</i>&quot; or &quot;<i>In our real modern world, extracted wealth is why developed countries have high levels of income today!</i>&quot;. Part of that's just the game world being a place I can take somewhat seriously.<br /> <br /> Also no weird asymmetries where it feels a bit like &quot;<i>When Dragonblooded do empire, it's all about material greed and in need of condemnation.... but if you want to rock out being empire-building Solar Alexander the Great, that's obviously legitimate and cool</i>&quot;. If we're criticizing empires and empires as a form of state in general rather than the political basis of the Scarlet Dynasty in specifics, let's be consistent in our condemnation.<br /> <br /> Then finally, needs a bit of consideration of &quot;<i>Yes, if you get rid of the Realm, you are going to have lots of would be local powers crop up and try and fill their vacuum, rather than nice little kind of democratic 'free peoples' or whatever, and lots of those local powers are going to be less competent at fighting the Fair Folk and managing predatory gods and the like</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Does 3e do a good job of all this? Undecided and I'd have to think about it some more.<br /> <br /> In edition terms, I kind of feel like First got away with all this much better than of the later commentary, though perhaps only because it mostly avoided a lot of these questions and offering specific answers, for better or worse. The flip side is that this can be less useful if you don't want to fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> On thread in general, feels like a lot of the common theme of points raised pro and con Third haven't really shifted much since the edition first dropped; mainly mechanics bloat (lots of Charms, lots of resources to manage, lots of interactions) combined with lack of opponents / 'ST tools' in general.<br /> <br /> In a way that's good, as it's better than &quot;<i>The mechanics actually implode under use</i>&quot;, but in a way that's a shame (for those who are experiencing Cons) because Third seems like it's on such a much longer cycle than previous editions, so you're stuck with what you've got.<br /> <br /> We're not moved on to a lot of &quot;<i>This looked like a problem before I started playing, but actually no problem</i>&quot;, and really what looked like it would be difficult or useful at the start of the edition still is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T15:23:51-08:00","id":1285408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285348#post1285348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was with Captain... Barbus? Barbar? I can't remember their name exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barbus, yes. Once we got to the Wyld Hunt story arc, pretty much everyone was captain of their own vessel. Admiral Misu was the one who really shone in naval maneuvers, though, as he took Sail Supernal. Given that he took Invincible Admiral Method, he was even able to help the others shine even with their relatively tiny commitments in Sail.<br /> <br /> Barbus' preferred tactic during naval combat was to try and not use the naval combat rules; given his investments in Athletics, Brawl, and Resistance, he was much more comfortable swimming or jumping over to the enemy ship and either engaging their crew or trying to punch a hole below the waterline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285348#post1285348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you like about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there were a number of moving parts that made it feel reasonably authentic. Sailing scenes in movies often bug me; two vessels might come at each other from opposite directions, <i>both</i> somehow running with the wind. <br /> <br /> (Yeah, that's right, Disney - I'm calling you out!)<br /> <br /> The rules for maneuvers also felt complete enough while still leaving room for tactics that the writers might not have thought of.<br /> <br /> I also liked that you couldn't farm fishing boats for Momentum to smash the big pirate frigate with. I get why they let you do it in the combat system, but there's frequently fewer ships in play in a naval scenes than there are combatants in a combat scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-06-2019, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T15:37:22-08:00","id":1285410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285408#post1285408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Yeah, that's right, Disney - I'm calling you out!)</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you looking at particularly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T15:43:32-08:00","id":1285411,"title":"","content":"Things I've done to make running Ex 3 a smoother process (having had experience running both prior editions).<ul><li><u>I created my own Charm file</u>, including Charm trees, for myself and the players. The Charms are all reduced to their mechanical basics, based on Irked's reworking. When a player uses a Charm, I can Ctrl-F to it quickly as needed. I can add or house rule Charms freely and excise those I dislike. The file also highlights a variety of rulings from the Devs and includes my own homebrew systems.</li> <li><u>Weaker starting Solars</u>. I decreased the number of starting Charms by a handful, and no Artifacts were allowed. Next game, I'll probably only grant half the Excellencies, in order to make the early game more challenging. The power level out of the gate renders most published challenges useless.</li> <li><u>Created a combat tracker.</u> I somehow acquired an old sheaf of (I think) accounting sheets. Initiatives at the top, crash to the side, and room in the middle for figures. Markers track initiative and are adjusted for having acted. All players can see it easily, and combat is far more manageable thereby.</li> <li><u>Ditched Solar xp mechanics</u>. I still give Solar xp, but after playing a couple sessions by the RAW, I tossed that system aside.</li> <li>I started the game in a <u>remote location</u> with its own problems. Three nations are in a Vale geographically isolated from its neighbors. In between is an unnatural forest, Devil-Tree, from which horrors emerge. Constraining Devil-tree is part of Vale culture, a way of life. But of late it's grown more active... Two PC's Exalted in the Riverlands and fled the Wyld Hunt, arriving in the Vale. Two other PC's were from opposed Vale nations. Banded together, their war against Devil-Tree became an epic tale that didn't rely on the lack of other splats, with non-Solar Exalts making only memorable cameos, their natures not really understood by the PC's.</li> <li><u>I rely on a diversity of problems</u>. Combat has remained a challenge, to some extent, because I've homebrewed most of their antagonists. But disease, poison, potential corruption from Devil-tree's minions, and multiple moral quandaries have kept things fresh and challenging.</li> </ul><br /> The biggest con for me at this point is the eventual challenge of running a combat with multiple Exalted antagonists that takes advantage of their Charm sets. I don't want to simplify things <i>too</i> much. The lack of other quality opponents is likewise problematic. I don't have time to homebrew the entire Exalted world.<br /> <br /> But my friends (3/5 of which were new to Exalted with this chronicle) and I do love this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T16:19:57-08:00","id":1285422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285410#post1285410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you looking at particularly?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Pirates of the Carribean: At World's End</i> in particular was the source of my specific example, but I could probably have gone with any number of movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-06-2019, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T16:32:18-08:00","id":1285426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285405#post1285405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No &quot;<i>In general, implausibly high, economically impossible levels of wealth are typically extracted under empires, keeping parts of empires that aren't the core at vastly different, vastly lower, wealth levels</i>&quot; or &quot;<i>In our real modern world, extracted wealth is why developed countries have high levels of income today!</i>&quot;. Part of that's just the game world being a place I can take somewhat seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on these two ideas a bit? Cause, uh... I don't understand why they strain credulity, as the former is historically accurate (in aggregate, there are exceptions, queue the Mongoltage, etcetc), and the later is both fundamentally true and seems immaterial when depiciting the consequences of imperial activity in a bronze/iron age setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T17:56:56-08:00","id":1285444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285143#post1285143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should also mention that our group had major problems with this as well until we came up with physical solutions, so that should factor into my pro/cons. A particularly crafty member of our group, like in real life, build a little board with moveable tiles and a big double-wide number line for initiative. Now whenever we go into combat a tile with each of our names on it goes onto the board and a tile with enemies A to up to G gets placed too. That way whenever we shuffle anything around it becomes obvious if they need to take an immediate turn, or how deadly the foe's current initiative is at. We tend to use Theatre of the Mind, so it takes the place of a combat map.<br /> <br /> Also we have two forms of morte/willpower counting for the taste of the player in question. One is an abacus with several different sections and colours that you can shuffle around for each of those pools. Another is a 4 section subdivided box, with larger coloured beads, and pools for willpower, personal, peripheral, and discarded motes. That way you also get the visceral feeling of picking up a mitt full of motes and willpower and tumbling them into the &quot;Spent&quot; box before pulling off your epic move.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree entirely.<br /> <br /> One of my players built a wooden battlewheel. It's even got spots around the edge for pegs, so we can note when upcoming events are about to happen. (&quot;IT'S GONNA BLOW!&quot;) We've also got cups &amp; trays out for our momentum (aka initiative) pools. <br /> <br /> We're working on getting together some better play sheets, laid out for counting out motes. <br /> <br /> No matter which system, the tactile counting is just about a must.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T18:33:04-08:00","id":1285451,"title":"","content":"If it's just personal stuff then I can take a crack at it<br /> Pros:<br /> Beefed up charm trees: Okay let me get this out of the way with, I'm a freak and an outlier, I fully acknowledge this, and I would unironically leap to play an edition of exalted where every single ability had fifty charms. What drew me to exalted in the first place was the breadth of the mechanics, that in theory each ability had just as much investment opportunity as the next. And what kept me from ever really getting into either of the previous editions was the fact that that wasn't really true. The combat abilities had big meaty charm sets and everything else usually hovered at six or so. The fact that I can actually invest my character into being a spy or a sailing merchant or a scholar, rather then just a swordsman who also does some of those things on the side, is probably the single largest thing I like about the game and the reason it's still my favorite. I fully realize I'm at odds with a lot of other peoples perceptions of the game, but hey there it is<br /> <br /> Social system: Third has the best social system I've seen in just about anything. It manages to balance the problem most other games run into of either being to ineffectual to be worth it, to powerful, and still managing to at least somehow model how real life humans interact.<br /> <br /> Evocations: Another place I get to wallow in my crunchy mess, evocations fit the ideal of epic mythology much better, where each weapon is it's own unique existence that differs from all other. Far harder to write sure but as stated above, I'm the type of weirdo who likes that.<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> The core book is cramped: It's no secret that there was some troubled history going on behind the core book. This compounds the fact that the core needed so much inside it already, setting info, the entirety of the beefed up base systems, an entire charm set, a collection of antagonists, all the item rules with a couple sample evocation sets, and multiple martial arts trees. They just didn't have room for everything, and some of the Troubles made things even more cramped. You can see frayed edges in a few places, incomplete mechanics around a couple of spots, so on.<br /> <br /> Schedule: Much related to the first one, these Troubles have kept things from ever hitting a solid pace, but the point I'm making here is more then just having to wait. Yeah that's a bummer no doubt, but I'm talking things beside that. The slow crawl has done noticeable things to the general mode surrounding the game, and means most of the material we have has already been walked all over by the time new things start to come out. Hopefully part of this gets alleviated when the ball actually gets rolling, but it won't change that the core got isolated on it's own for entire years counting the leaks and picked to pieces before we had anything else to pay attention to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T19:15:24-08:00","id":1285457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285370#post1285370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 1e presented the game much better in a neutral tone there are a lot of things I don't like about 3E and the removal of the neutral tone and feeling like there are inherent biases by the authors is one of them. 2E had that issue as well but the tone between 2E and 3E have been very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree with this. A lot of things that are better handled matter-of-fact are lingered upon and put on pedestals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T20:44:16-08:00","id":1285468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285405#post1285405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also no weird asymmetries where it feels a bit like &quot;<i>When Dragonblooded do empire, it's all about material greed and in need of condemnation.... but if you want to rock out being empire-building Solar Alexander the Great, that's obviously legitimate and cool</i>&quot;. If we're criticizing empires and empires as a form of state in general rather than the political basis of the Scarlet Dynasty in specifics, let's be consistent in our condemnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not sure if this is so much a thing that books do, as players do. I've seen a load of games, in fact it might even be most exalted games that I've seen, have either been about taking control of the Realm, or tearing off it's head and replacing it. The assumption, I think, being that they will make the empire righteous and pure and fair and good and all that. On the flip side I'm not sure I've ever played in a game where the PCs have struggled to create a network of local governments with elected officials or anything.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's a thing the books have ever implied is easy to do though, making a good empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T21:38:16-08:00","id":1285475,"title":"","content":"I propose that, fifteen years ago, a neutral tone concerning the subject of gay and trans rights and media representation was a luxury that has been kind of lost in the intervening time. <br /> <br /> If, fifteen years from now, it's a luxury that becomes reclaimed (hopefully under better circumstances than it existed in the past), I doubt I'll complain about it.<br /> <br /> But it's not the environment we're currently in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T04:57:51-08:00","id":1285531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285426#post1285426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate on these two ideas a bit? Cause, uh... I don't understand why they strain credulity, as the former is historically accurate (in aggregate, there are exceptions, queue the Mongoltage, etcetc), and the later is both fundamentally true and seems immaterial when depiciting the consequences of imperial activity in a bronze/iron age setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long tangent incoming:<br /> <br /> Re; first point, the former depends on what we're defining as vastly different, vastly lower levels of wealth. My definition tends to be that a vast difference in wealth is something like the &quot;developed&quot; and &quot;developing&quot; world in 1960 or 1890, and I tend to think that's something like modern people's go to for the scales implied by that kind of phrasing.<br /> <br /> But the economic argument is that it's never been possible to extract from poor countries to achieve that kind of gap, because there isn't enough money to transfer, and the logistics of doing so are impossible. Assume if country A is at $600 GDP and B is at $700 GDP, equal population size, then even transferring 50% of income from A to B is only going to put A at $1000 GDP. And of course transfers were waaaaay less than 50% in any case, very much lower; not every one in two, probably far less than every one in ten - most people are subsistence farmers after all (not people with much available wealth to spare in any form). Assuming equal population size, but doesn't change too much if population size is non-equal, particularly for a demographic juggernaut like the Realm (even in 3e's bigger world, I believe it still is?).<br /> <br /> (E.g. Britain in India, where there is a smaller imperial power vs larger colonised territory, extracted tax rate about 7.5% of national income - <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/yaewytjo\" target=\"_blank\">https://tinyurl.com/yaewytjo</a>. Most of which they would've had to spend in the country, on armies, administration, some nominal public works, etc.)<br /> <br /> Look at the Inequality Possibility Frontier for practice - <a href=\"https://www.gc.cuny.edu/CUNY_GC/media/CUNY-Graduate-Center/PDF/Centers/LIS/Milanovic/papers/2013/WPS6449.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gc.cuny.edu/CUNY_GC/medi...13/WPS6449.pdf</a>. Part of that argument is also that large extraction did take place, it would push many people below subsistence.<br /> <br /> Even Spanish and Portuguese colonization of the Americas, probably an extreme of extraction, barely or did not at all push their national incomes up. There's no change in GDP/capita estimates - <a href=\"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/maddison-data-gdp-per-capita-in-2011us-single-benchmark?country=FRA+ESP+PRT\" target=\"_blank\">https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/m...ry=FRA+ESP+PRT</a><br /> <br /> Some idea of what was possible for Rome is here: <a href=\"https://brilliantmaps.com/roman-empire-gdp/\" target=\"_blank\">https://brilliantmaps.com/roman-empire-gdp/</a>, and even then the lion's share of the difference is driven by the poor nature of the northern provinces (which is in turn primarily due to lower trade and stock of techniques and knowledge, and environment constraints).<br /> <br /> In terms of the &quot;wealth of nations&quot; for empires, figuratively, through most of history, you're largely talking about two desperately poor beggars fighting in an alley, and one maybe gets a few pennies from the other, but they remain desperately poor. Or a rich thug rifling through the pockets of a poor man, but he's rich regardless of doing so. Rather than anyone getting rich from stealing. In a narrower scale, a few individuals can get rich and have marvelous estates, even then though they're often not the same ones bearing the cost of the empire, so looking at those in isolation in the context of the general poverty around them overstates things, and that nothing much has happened to the national income.<br /> <br /> Of course, these relatively small amounts can matter to *them*! And it is still a sense some vast cultural outrage when treasures are dragged off to adorn a imperial administrator's house.<br /> <br /> Re; second point, consensus usually is that the transition to modern economic growth in late 1700s and then 1800s both explains income gaps today and has nothing much to do with taxation / loot / plantations in colonies and empires. Rather changes in practices rooted in legal, economic, scientific changes that don't really have much to do with them.<br /> <br /> Some econ historians allow some small measure of savings from colonial enterprises contributed to investment, but my impression is that this is mostly a sop, and that the most rigorous writers emphasise that growth in industries (seen across all industries and driving change) was mostly driven by savings driven investment and invention and shifting labour and had nothing really to do with colonial profits.<br /> <br /> But that's all I'll do here, as that's an element that you can just search and pretty much any result on economic history on economic growth will tell you, so not much point me trying to reproduce here, risking getting some small element of the argument wrong (and then &quot;de-convincing&quot; anyone reading who wants to believe the opposite and is ill disposed to the way I've phrased things and their feel of any subtext they might think they find.).<br /> <br /> I agree it shouldn't have much to do with the setting writing! I'm reacting a bit to an old dialogue about an impression I got that early 3e team wanted to use the Realm to say something about imperialism in the recent past and legacies in world today. But I don't get this impression from the current team, so I'm probably at risk of shading from useful (or at least thread relevant) points into a useless sort of &quot;Ghosthead shouts at things that people who aren't even here now said, years ago, that probably have no relevance today, and that no one's talking about ITT!&quot; here to go any further.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, you're probably right about it being more of a player dependent element and I'm risking a bit straying into &quot;Somebody, somewhere, not even in this thread, let alone in the books, is *wrong* on (or off) the internet&quot; territory here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T05:14:53-08:00","id":1285534,"title":"","content":"I read a paper the other day that calculated that the Empire created about 17% of Britain's economic growth between 1800 and 1900.<br /> So, it's some of it, but not most.<br /> <br /> Though, as you mention, that doesn't mean individuals weren't getting fantastically rich (or, incidentally, that it didn't devastate subject economies. Sending people to conquer and fight wars is not a net economic positive. Or even neutral).<br /> <br /> I'm sure that the Realm does extract a lot of wealth from satrapies, making the Dynasty rich, that's why they do it. But at the end of the day, Realm peasants are richer than Threshold peasants mostly because they have better soil, better weather, and don't get invaded by Dragonblood as often. Sure, it's nice when your son brings back loot from the Threshold, but it doesn't make a huge difference compared to if he'd stayed home and you didn't have to pay taxes to support invasions.<br /> (It's probably something like... 17% better.)<br /> <br /> It's probably worth noting that while I agree with Ghosthead's general point (not every detail, but the overall point), this is a contraversial topic amongst historians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-07-2019, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T06:02:58-08:00","id":1285539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285531#post1285531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DrLoveMonkey, you're probably right about it being more of a player dependent element and I'm risking a bit straying into &quot;Somebody, somewhere, not even in this thread, let alone in the books, is *wrong* on (or off) the internet&quot; territory here</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s not something worth talking about though, especially with how maybe it seems like that might be changing in third edition. Or at least the writers making more prominent that even solar heroes might end up just replacing one form of oppression with another, and how players might feel about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T06:16:56-08:00","id":1285541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285531#post1285531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the economic argument is that it's never been possible to extract from poor countries to achieve that kind of gap, because there isn't enough money to transfer, and the logistics of doing so are impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>....<br /> <br /> When the English had control of Ireland, they weren't taking our &quot;money&quot;.<br /> <br /> They were taking our food. Which they sold to other English people.<br /> <br /> Taking our food was so important that they sent armed escorts for it, lest starving farmers and their children have the audacity to think that a simple thing like famine entitle them to the fruits of their homeland.<br /> <br /> The American colonies provided tobacco and cotton. The Caribbean, sugar. India had tea. Various African colonies produced coffee, popular tropical fruits, and various minerals that were valued for appearance or industrial application.<br /> <br /> Now, as getting actual liquid cash goes, that tends to consist of the disparity in industrialisation; Britain takes the raw materials, converts them to manufactured goods, and sells them back to the empire at high prices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:06:10-08:00","id":1285567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285468#post1285468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually not sure if this is so much a thing that books do, as players do. I've seen a load of games, in fact it might even be most exalted games that I've seen, have either been about taking control of the Realm, or tearing off it's head and replacing it. The assumption, I think, being that they will make the empire righteous and pure and fair and good and all that. On the flip side I'm not sure I've ever played in a game where the PCs have struggled to create a network of local governments with elected officials or anything.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's a thing the books have ever implied is easy to do though, making a good empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm... well sometimes the books do it (the Solars are righteous true kings who will save Creation), but not a ton. Less than people on forums, certainly.<br /> <br /> Personally, I always felt that Solars were somewhat a deconstruction of Rightful Kings anyway (hence the wonderful text of the 2e Larceny Charms. Like &quot;It is the Lawgiver's right to confiscate goods necessary to the service of the Unconquered Sun&quot; for pickpocketing, or &quot;Only the unrighteous would lock a door to keep the Solars out. Such an intention is proof of iniquity&quot; for the charm for breaking into people's houses. This developed into my Twilight telling our Night that when he stole things, that's not theft, it's Solar Tax, so it's fine). But other people seem to take them more seriously.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, the tension between &quot;conquer yourself an Empire&quot; and &quot;encourage countries to righteously rule themselves&quot; is a common theme (and tension) in the games I play.<br /> <br /> In one game, we overthrew the government of Coral and helped set up a new, less sexist, more democratic government that would no longer throw people to sharks.<br /> Then we travelled to Harborhead (it was a long trip) where we drove out the Autocthonian invaders and freed the Harborheadians.<br /> We hung out with Ahlat a bit, then headed to Sukhmet, the Egyptian-esque land of the Night Caste's birth.<br /> After various other things, we spent some time in the neighbouring Empire. We slew the evil war-mongering Emperor, replaced him with a Lunar doppleganger (me and my character's daughter took turns), and put a set of philosophers (we had a philosophy competition, and chose the nicest ones. The Mohists, rather than the Legalists) and a nice Dragon King (who'd been imprisoned by his fellows for being too pro-human and anti-human sacrifice) as regents while the Emperor &quot;went into seclusion&quot;. We also announced the war against the northern rebels was over.<br /> <br /> Then we went back to Sukhmet, and here the tension came in, as the Night Caste was adopted as a &quot;long-lost son&quot; by the Pharoah, and married his daugher. At this point, the party got soft on the whole overthrowing-monarchs thing, unsurprisingly.<br /> Though the Night did kill his adopted brother, an Abyssal, so he couldn't inherit the throne (and now the Night has run off to become a righteous folk hero of the streets, as being a Prince is too stressful), and the nicer brother became Pharoah.<br /> Of course, he's still a Pharoah, so supporting a fundamentally unfair system. The other Night (whose Defining Intimacy is &quot;killing tyrants&quot;) is thinking about whether to overthrow him or not. Him and the Changing Moon would like to make the first Night Pharoah, but he doesn't want to (as he doesn't feel he's qualified to be Pharoah).<br /> The Changing Moon, originally an anarchist who killed slavers, seems to have lost her anti-authoritan convictions now she's a pampered concubine of a Prince. Who'd have thought?<br /> <br /> <br /> In the other game I play, the PCs overthrew all kinds of oppressive regimes, and encouraged more democratic regimes, or put commoners on the throne as they'd understood the common people more.<br /> But over time I'd say they got a bit more ends-justify-the-means. Sometimes they appointed rulers who, well, they liked, but weren't necessarily good, because the better rulers were more hostile to them. And they also, as you can tell, got more into &quot;appointing rulers&quot; and less into &quot;seeing what the common people wanted.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now the main tension is that two PCs are very keen on forging their own kingdoms (through conquest, trade, and magical loyalty), while the others are violently opposed to the concept (with Defining Intimacies like &quot;No Gods and No Masters&quot;). Yet the first two see the others as hypocrites (somewhat fairly), because their goals of religious freedom, forging alliances rather than conquest, encouraging local autonomy, etc, sometimes seem to involve things like brutal coups and assassinations, and generally actions that don't always look that different from the two conquerers. And the religious freedom is mostly about the religion of those &quot;freedom-loving&quot; PCs. Though the slaves rescued by the Zenith obviously do see them as quite different from the racist tyrant Dawn who was selling them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-07-2019, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:55:26-08:00","id":1285578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285451#post1285451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What drew me to exalted in the first place was the breadth of the mechanics, that in theory each ability had just as much investment opportunity as the next. And what kept me from ever really getting into either of the previous editions was the fact that that wasn't really true. The combat abilities had big meaty charm sets and everything else usually hovered at six or so. The fact that I can actually invest my character into being a spy or a sailing merchant or a scholar, rather then just a swordsman who also does some of those things on the side, is probably the single largest thing I like about the game and the reason it's still my favorite. I fully realize I'm at odds with a lot of other peoples perceptions of the game, but hey there it is</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you there, to some extent.<br /> <br /> Along with a much better setting than any of DnD's published ones, the fact that your character can be an amazing bureaucrat/author/public speaker/detective rather than just a master of combat who is also good at some other stuff, is why I still like Exalted after all these years, compared to DnD/Runequest/Pathfinder/L5R/whatever.<br /> <br /> Some of the beefed-up charm trees I don't enjoy, because I think they're beefed up with boring/weak stuff (like Craft and Presence).<br /> But others, like Investigation, are real improvements from 2nd ed, that used to just have 5 or 6 charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:55:34-08:00","id":1285595,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s interesting and hasn\u2019t been my experience at all, even through multiple different groups. The closest we had was probably a group that kind of half overthrew a satrapy. It started in the middle of the desert, running low on water because the magical water screws were breaking down. A rebellion was forming because the nobles were keeping enough water for themselves* while the poor wallowed in dry, disease filled streets. A particularly angry group of young men decided that if they couldn\u2019t have water, nobody could. So aided by half the party they went and blew up the remaining water screws, opposed by the other half of the party. Anyway long story short a demon invasion was summoned into the city, by a corrupt Dynast, killed most of the other Dynasts and took over the city. The PCs assaulted the palace aided by their rebel allies, killed the demons and then manipulated a Realm legion into cleaning the streets for them. By the end of it they were kind of running the satrapy from the shadows behind the new satrap. From there they used Solar night to restore the city to its lost glory and made lives better for the lower classes. I think that\u2019s as close as I\u2019ve ever seen a group get to overthrowing a tyrant without taking over themselves. Every other campaign is either running around fighting horrors, conquering the world with your own empire, or being a Dynast. The last one usually ends up being either just everyone playing bastards or everyone trying to use what little influence they have to alleviate some of the bad stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Which is to say they all had plenty to drink, and some of the more altruistic ones were even giving up the occasional bath to divert some water to the lower levels of the city, which they thought was quite generous indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T10:09:46-08:00","id":1285601,"title":"","content":"I don't think I have ever played a game with everyone happy to conquer, except Dynastic games. Often there's one or two Solars who do want to, but the others reign them in and focus on fighting evil instead. (I had a Twilight sorcerer, Shadow of Kings, whose motivation was Rule the World. Then he lost all his Solar powers, had memory problems, and his Raksha girlfriend vanished. We went to rescue her, and discovered she'd been kidnapped by... Shadow of Kings! He'd got fed up that the others wouldn't let him conquer anything, and also kept calling him fat, so he ran off to join the party's enemy and left behind a biomotonic replicant in his place.)<br /> <br /> I guess it just depends on the players.<br /> After playing a lot of Vampire and Dragonblood, I think when we started playing Solars, we wanted to be heroes.<br /> <br /> Though things could have been quite different if the Yeddim-riding mercenary general and mercenary Dawn caste hadn't died in the first arc and been replaced with a naieve street kid and an engineer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-07-2019, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T16:17:08-08:00","id":1285714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1284882#post1284882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's because it would otherwise take only three starting Charm slots to become capable of melting cities from the word go. That's both a much shorter path than any other Supernal needs, and kind of has a more profound impact than any Supernal besides Lore (which is a lot more restricted in mass destruction than sorcery is).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something you can deal with by just adding more prerequisites. There were options they could have explored on that, but did not, and I would have preferred if they had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T03:48:10-08:00","id":1285843,"title":"","content":"Pros<br /> <br /> 1) Fantastic setting, goes without saying<br /> 2) Core combat system is absolutely excellent<br /> 3) Intimacies and Social System also absolutely excellent<br /> 4) extremely evocative and imagery-laden mechanics for Exalted making you feel like a demigod<br /> 5) Evocations are hugely cool<br /> 6) Massive excision of magitech as a concept from setting makes the 1st age and it's artifacts wondrous again<br /> <br /> Cons<br /> <br /> 1) Bloated combat. So many charms, interactions, elements to track etc. It's a bloody nightmare to run and keep going at a brisk exciting pace once you get into a combat between multiple exalted, rolling hundreds of dice a round and marking of motes, willpower, health levels, applying half a dozen charm effects, running calculations... Yeah. It's a fucking nightmare. It's the hardest combat to run of almost any game ever. <br /> 2) This is compounded by a complete lack of decent GM resources in the core. Huge amounts of useless stuff, very little that's Solar campaign relevant. This is something they're absolutely trying to resolve though, which is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T10:02:39-08:00","id":1285939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285843#post1285843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pros<br /> 1) Bloated combat. So many charms, interactions, elements to track etc. It's a bloody nightmare to run and keep going at a brisk exciting pace once you get into a combat between multiple exalted, rolling hundreds of dice a round and marking of motes, willpower, health levels, applying half a dozen charm effects, running calculations... Yeah. It's a fucking nightmare. It's the hardest combat to run of almost any game ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this to both be true and not true. The combat system is rather snappy when you are playing mortals. I have also noticed that combat is still fairly quick with dragon blooded because they don't have as bad of bloat. Also, while I do respect the work of the past developers, DB charms are wrote much clearer and cleaner. <br /> <br /> What I found that really helped was to print out the charms on card stock and make my own charm cards. Additionally in our group it is expected that you are formulating and planing on the person's turn before you then have everything figured out by the start of yours which makes things a lot quicker. <br /> <br /> All that said having played with a martial arts supernal dawn though I get what you are saying, when you are laying out huge numbers of charms all that once it can get confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T11:53:39-08:00","id":1285974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285939#post1285939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this to both be true and not true. The combat system is rather snappy when you are playing mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really surprise me.<br /> <br /> Recording initiative, health, wp (which you don't use that much) and onslaught (which resets every turn, normally, and for PCs often is just 1) is actually okay, I find.<br /> But then, with Exalts, you also have to record Motes, which regenerate every turn, and Anima.<br /> Then of course, there's the charms. And the more you have, the harder it is. In the game I play, most characters have 35-40 charms.<br /> <br /> Certainly, when my players make mistakes or get confused, it's normally about charms, not the basic combat rules.<br /> <br /> Still, there's Solar charms and there's Solar charms. Some are more complex than others. Some trees are more complex than others.<br /> I really wish the ones who are bad at remembering their charms would just go big on Ox-bodies rather than combine +1 success, re-roll 1s, re-rolls 6s until they no longer appear, double 9s, etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ox-bodies are easy to remember.<br /> <br /> I have also found that PCs with, say, 5 combat charms/5 craft charms/5 social charms/5 investigation charms are way easier for players to get their head around than characters with 25 combat charms or 25 social charms or 25 craft charms.<br /> You have to remember as many charms... but not at the same time, and you don't have to think much about how to combine them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All that said having played with a martial arts supernal dawn though I get what you are saying </div> </div> </div>I think a Dawn who combines multiple martial arts has to be one of the hardest characters to run. I made a character with multiple martial arts, and I've had to work out how they work in combo and write those seperately from the actual charms. It looks a bit overwhelming.<br /> I haven't actually got into a fight though, yet.<br /> <br /> I think the only thing that might be harder would be a Dawn who just has 30 Melee charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have also noticed that combat is still fairly quick with dragon blooded because they don't have as bad of bloat. Also, while I do respect the work of the past developers, DB charms are wrote much clearer and cleaner. </div> </div> </div>They seemed so to me, though I've not actually played one.<br /> <br /> I have a friend who runs a Dragonblood game, I asked him how he found 3rd ed DBs. He said generally good, but most of the players couldn't get their heads around Aura so avoided stuff that was based around it. Except for two players (one who's good at mechanics except for occasional weird interpretations, and one who isn't but I guess went for a very straight-forward character with one Aura) who are therefore using a whole bunch of cool, awesome powers that the others don't have.<br /> <br /> How have you found Aura? My friends told me they found it a bit fiddly (except for the first guy I mentioned), but looking at the rules I think it depends how the character is built. Though still a bit fiddly for everyone.<br /> As I said though, I haven't actually played a DB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-08-2019, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T12:18:34-08:00","id":1285981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285974#post1285974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have also found that PCs with, say, 5 combat charms/5 craft charms/5 social charms/5 investigation charms are way easier for players to get their head around than characters with 25 combat charms or 25 social charms or 25 craft charms.<br /> <br /> You have to remember as many charms... but not at the same time, and you don't have to think much about how to combine them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to maybe say something say something controversial, but I think supernal was a mistake, for this reason. It results in over specialization. The only reason I had a easy time was because I was a craft supernal and made a script like is x happens activate y charm to add w amounts of gold experience and the like. Also I had other sub themes I also wanted to put lots of charms in so it worked out alright. But let\u2019s NOT make this about the craft system destroyer of threads shall we?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285974#post1285974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How have you found Aura? My friends told me they found it a bit fiddly (except for the first guy I mentioned), but looking at the rules I think it depends how the character is built. Though still a bit fiddly for everyone.<br /> <br /> As I said though, I haven't actually played a DB.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it easy, but only because I am playing a wood aspect hunter that is an archer on a mount. Basically I have decided to make my life easy and only buy wood and balanced charms for combat. So there is never a reason for me not to be in wood aura in combat. In other situations (social mostly) I find it pretty easy to keep track of and I don\u2019t think I have any charms that need it anyway outside of tracking and shooting people with arrows.<br /> <br /> Other players have other methods. One guy just has glass beads he changes out that he keeps on his character sheet and another has a dice.<br /> I personally don\u2019t find it to be that big of a deal.<br /> <br /> You should play a DB, they are fun, but I also prefer a lower power level. Another controversial view is I find Solars to be a bit over powered honestly. The game has all these cool little subsystems and whirlygigs to play with and most of the Solar charms are so strong that they basically kick them to the curb. They are so good I actually find them a bit boring. Preferences are preferences though so take all that as you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 02-08-2019, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T12:51:01-08:00","id":1285989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285981#post1285981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other players have other methods. One guy just has glass beads he changes out that he keeps on his character sheet and another has a dice.<br /> I personally don\u2019t find it to be that big of a deal.<br /> <br /> You should play a DB, they are fun, but I also prefer a lower power level. Another controversial view is I find Solars to be a bit over powered honestly. The game has all these cool little subsystems and whirlygigs to play with and most of the Solar charms are so strong that they basically kick them to the curb. They are so good I actually find them a bit boring. Preferences are preferences though so take all that as you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that has to be done slowly, if Wizard\u2019s group goes from Essence 5 Solars to Essence 2 DBs they might die of shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T13:01:30-08:00","id":1285992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285989#post1285989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that has to be done slowly, if Wizard\u2019s group goes from Essence 5 Solars to Essence 2 DBs they might die of shock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Maybe! Or maybe it would be a breath of fresh air. The current game (currently on hiatus) we were playing we started out as mortal dynasts going on a huge dangerous adventure. We were all reaching the age where one just gives up on being 'blessed by the dragons' but we went about putting ourselves in great danger hoping to ignite that spark inside of ourselves (basically waiting for the KS). Which we did (after the KS ended). I have to say that I it was quite the power boost becoming dragon blooded from mortals and a good way to learn the system. I have to say I am much more comfortable with the whole system now compared to the first time we played when we jumped right into Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:03:49-08:00","id":1286009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285989#post1285989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that has to be done slowly, if Wizard\u2019s group goes from Essence 5 Solars to Essence 2 DBs they might die of shock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most of them actually also play an Essence 3 Dragonblood game. But it has like 7 players already, and is on weekdays, so I don't play it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd love to play a low Essence game, possibly DBs. I'm sick of high Essence and high XP, and I'm a little bit sick of Solars. (I'm not sick of the plot of the 2 Exalted games I play, so I keep playing, but if the ST had a magical vortex that sucked out all the PCs XP I wouldn't complain.)<br /> It's just that my playgroup loves their characters too much to start a new game. When I stopped running my Essence 5 game, two of them immediately volunteered to run it so they could all carry on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to maybe say something say something controversial, but I think supernal was a mistake, for this reason. It results in over specialization.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's quite a few people who agree with you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I haven't found it to be a problem so far. When I made a starting Solar (for a game that sadly didn't get off the ground) I only took 7 charms from my Supernal, because I needed other stuff, and so Supernal just meant I wasn't restricted to the first 4 charms of the tree. But with only 7 charms, I think the highest was Essence 2.<br /> <br /> But, while I haven't seen people abuse it, I can definitely imagine that you can if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game has all these cool little subsystems and whirlygigs to play with and most of the Solar charms are so strong that they basically kick them to the curb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think all of the Solar charms are like that... (Actually, I find it a little amusing how difficult our Zenith finds social influence because the Presence tree mostly isn't actually very good at kicking the subsystems to the curb... The DB Presence tree is better at it, if technically weaker.)<br /> <br /> But Craft absolutely is, and you said that's the one you had Supernal.<br /> I mean, there was a point at which I gave up making the Crafter count his Craft XP, because he generated about 30 gold xp a day just be being him. My own crafter generates a ton of Crafting XP I just don't use; there's no real need to generate a few measly more silver or gold by actually engaging with the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should play a DB, they are fun,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to, but there isn't really the opportunity.<br /> <br /> I recently made a new character for the Essence 5 game we play, after my Night get Death Rayed, but it's a high-powered game where most of the PCs are members of the Cult of the Illuminated battling the Realm and other Dragonblood allies of the Realm, so I didn't think it would fit.<br /> <br /> In the other game I play (Essence 4), I don't love my Zenith that much, and I was planning to retire him and play a DB (it would fit really well there), but the plot we're doing now is one that my Zenith is really involved in (and while I don't love him, I do really like the plot). I was going to retire him after this arc, but the ST's going to put it on hiatus and run something else (the game's been going for 10 years. That, frankly, is enough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:26:18-08:00","id":1286019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1285714#post1285714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something you can deal with by just adding more prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely you then have people complaining about the need to invest in other Occult Charms infringing upon the variety and purity of their sorcerer character concepts.<br /> <br /> I'm not very far from that myself with some people's complaints about Dragon Blooded sorcery, but for my accepting the explanation that even the Terrestrial circle is proportionately powerful for them that there needs to be a bit of something preventing it from feeling like a bit of a default option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were options they could have explored on that, but did not, and I would have preferred if they had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exploring options is a thing done in the planning stages, not the final draft or published product. I don't doubt that there were alternative models that they considered before coming down on the final idea. Some of which might have been complicated when they had a very different idea about how sorcery was going to work.<br /> <br /> Robert Vance is our developer now, there's a thread for asking him questions, and he was pretty much <b>the</b> writer of sorcery. My comment came from an old explanation by Holden, but why not ask him directly what options were explored for sorcery and what he knows of why it came down as it did?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:28:06-08:00","id":1286020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286009#post1286009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think all of the Solar charms are like that... (Actually, I find it a little amusing how difficult our Zenith finds social influence because the Presence tree mostly isn't actually very good at kicking the subsystems to the curb... The DB Presence tree is better at it, if technically weaker.)<br /> <br /> But Craft absolutely is, and you said that's the one you had Supernal.<br /> I mean, there was a point at which I gave up making the Crafter count his Craft XP, because he generated about 30 gold xp a day just be being him. My own crafter generates a ton of Crafting XP I just don't use; there's no real need to generate a few measly more silver or gold by actually engaging with the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a fair assessment and I had much the same happen to me. I actually like the craft system for various reason but solar craft charms just make it too easy. To the point I retired my character for another concept because I felt like I was already the best in the world, why bother advancing further? That is all I care to say though; I have a lot of opinions on the solar craft charms and this isn't the place for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T15:38:03-08:00","id":1286034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286009#post1286009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, most of them actually also play an Essence 3 Dragonblood game. But it has like 7 players already, and is on weekdays, so I don't play it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd love to play a low Essence game, possibly DBs. I'm sick of high Essence and high XP, and I'm a little bit sick of Solars. (I'm not sick of the plot of the 2 Exalted games I play, so I keep playing, but if the ST had a magical vortex that sucked out all the PCs XP I wouldn't complain.)<br /> It's just that my playgroup loves their characters too much to start a new game. When I stopped running my Essence 5 game, two of them immediately volunteered to run it so they could all carry on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really too bad, my group got kind of tired of it too, so we swapped to DnD and it was indeed as Snakes said, a breath of fresh air. Players were cautious, worked hard to be ingenuitive, they were concerned with making/keeping alliances and planning. The total opposite of how they were acting as powerful Solars, which was basically to just see a problem and go after it with reckless abandon, solve it, pick next problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T23:24:53-08:00","id":1286101,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I started playing (and running) DnD again a couple of years ago, and I found it refreshing. So much simpler, well-balanced, etc. And the players don't push around every king, queen, god or chief they meet.<br /> <br /> But I'm starting to get bored of the combat system (which for my wizard, mostly consists of casting scorching ray or shatter again and again) and the lack of support for much else. It makes me appreciate Exalted. I'd just really like to play an Exalted game where people have 15 charms, not 40, and thus can remember them.<br /> Oh, and where people haven't maxed most of their pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-09-2019, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T05:27:09-08:00","id":1286150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286101#post1286101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just really like to play an Exalted game where people have 15 charms, not 40, and thus can remember them.<br /> Oh, and where people haven't maxed most of their pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you use Discord? Message me if you do. I wouldn't mind putting a game together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T05:54:18-08:00","id":1286154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286101#post1286101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I started playing (and running) DnD again a couple of years ago, and I found it refreshing. So much simpler, well-balanced, etc. And the players don't push around every king, queen, god or chief they meet.<br /> <br /> But I'm starting to get bored of the combat system (which for my wizard, mostly consists of casting scorching ray or shatter again and again) and the lack of support for much else. It makes me appreciate Exalted. I'd just really like to play an Exalted game where people have 15 charms, not 40, and thus can remember them.<br /> Oh, and where people haven't maxed most of their pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest issue with 3e is that a lot of them just add dice where they used to just give you the ability to do shit. It's even more annoying when they interconnect. It'd just be better to have personal combos that you rarely deviate from just to simplify the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T12:37:19-08:00","id":1286268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286101#post1286101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm starting to get bored of the combat system (which for my wizard, mostly consists of casting scorching ray or shatter again and again) and the lack of support for much else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of off-topic, but have you considered trying to do more buffing, debuffing, or battlefield control? I've always felt like the &quot;god wizard&quot; style of play where you fuck over your enemies by weakening or splitting them for your partymates to kill with swords, to be more satisfying than being a &quot;nuke wizard&quot; and just outputting damage, since you have to think a little more outside the box for tactical application of environmental stuff. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the D&amp;D rules are very much over-oriented for combat and a lot of the rest really comes down to, &quot;here are some skills, ask the DM to use them.&quot; If you have a good D&amp;D DM like I do, that means that social and mental skills come up frequently and can have real relevant impacts to solving issues, finding clues, making alliances, etc. For others, that may not be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T12:39:12-08:00","id":1286269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286154#post1286154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My biggest issue with 3e is that a lot of them just add dice where they used to just give you the ability to do shit. It's even more annoying when they interconnect. It'd just be better to have personal combos that you rarely deviate from just to simplify the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on this a bit? I'm not 100% sure what you're saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T12:53:36-08:00","id":1286272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286268#post1286268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of off-topic, but have you considered trying to do more buffing, debuffing, or battlefield control? I've always felt like the &quot;god wizard&quot; style of play where you fuck over your enemies by weakening or splitting them for your partymates to kill with swords, to be more satisfying than being a &quot;nuke wizard&quot; and just outputting damage, since you have to think a little more outside the box for tactical application of environmental stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll second that, also equipment can be really cool. Have the rogue scout ahead, find a couple of ogres there, hang back, setup a tripwire trap, scatter some caltrops on the other side of the trap and go goad the ogres into chasing her back through your little hallway of death. It's time the MONSTERS had to deal with traps for once! If you're a wizard, definitely pick up some illusion magic as well, you'd be shocked at how good it can be. You can make illusory terrain to give people concealment, have the enemies flee before an illusory dragon, or use Creation to make any random tool you might need. If this was a DnD forum I could make a whole thread about the new and interesting ways I'm finding to fight in 5e.<br /> <br /> <br /> The non-combat rules though are definitely lacking, and they're also something Exalted tends to do really well which makes the DnD ones seem even worse. As a GM it can be really difficult to pull off, but I try to make the best use I can out of the knowledge rolls and give appropriate bonuses for, effectively, targeting intimacies. I have actually run lots of political intrigue in it, but apart from a few spells or the thief infiltrating a palace to spy, the most important stat that ever came up were people's background choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T13:00:27-08:00","id":1286275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286268#post1286268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of off-topic, but have you considered trying to do more buffing, debuffing, or battlefield control? I've always felt like the &quot;god wizard&quot; style of play where you fuck over your enemies by weakening or splitting them for your partymates to kill with swords, to be more satisfying than being a &quot;nuke wizard&quot; and just outputting damage, since you have to think a little more outside the box for tactical application of environmental stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do a bit, but at level 4 I don't have a ton of options*. Sometimes I levitate enemies, but then the combat characters can't reach them. Also, one of the girls in the group is playing a bard, and she does a lot of buffing/debuffing/battlefield control (sleep, etc).<br /> (Also, my character is traumatised from what happened when he cast grease under an owlbear surrounded by children. He thought the owlbear would fall over and the children escape. They fell over, and the owlbear ripped them to pieces. He doesn't want to cast Grease again.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have a good D&amp;D DM like I do, that means that social and mental skills come up frequently and can have real relevant impacts to solving issues, finding clues, making alliances, etc. </div> </div> </div>We generally do 1 combat a session, max, and we do make a lot of non-combat skill checks. Our DM was big into theatre and improv, so interesting characters is more what she's interested in (though her combats tend to be well done too, not just 5 orcs in a white room).<br /> <br /> But the game doesn't support social characters with many interesting things to do besides &quot;have a high skill rating&quot;. Princess Evylyn rolls high rolls for diplomacy, Xenophon (my wizard) gets high rolls for knowledge, and Blaze rolls high for stealth and theft, but the game doesn't give us much to do with that beyond the skill checks. That's where Exalted stands out.<br /> <br /> *I do have various non-combat spells, because I find stuff like Invisibility fun. Having more than just &quot;big numbers on dice rolls&quot;** is why I'm playing a wizard. It's just, at the end of the day, when we're being attacked by shadow monsters, Scorching Ray is the best move.<br /> <br /> **Which, unfortunately, a fairly hefty portion of Solars charms are. Though some charm trees are better than others. I have a lot of Occult and Investigation charms on my Zenith, and they're very good generally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It'd just be better to have personal combos that you rarely deviate from just to simplify the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>For my 40-charm Lunar martial artist, I did write out a bunch of combos (like all the withering charms together, all the decisive charms together, etc). But then, sometimes you want to do less to save motes, so you need to write more combos, etc. Worth doing, but not perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-09-2019, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T09:26:43-08:00","id":1286468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286269#post1286269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you elaborate on this a bit? I'm not 100% sure what you're saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>In previous editions, most of the time moves just let you do something you couldn't do. Sometimes they gave you extra dice but that wasn't always the case. <br /> <br /> In this edition, the charmbloat is insane. You have 4-10x the charms you used to and most of them just seem to add dice. They make you better than normal but they're just a bridge rather than stepping stones to power. Getting the ability to attack twice isn't that great without all the other charms that boost the dice you roll. So you end up forming combos to do optimal damage. In addition,to that they added roll cascades and other tricks which slow combat down. You used to just get bucket of dice frontloaded with an undodgable attack. Now it's pieced out into several different phases on it's own. The new system is somewhat more balanced but it's also more obnoxious to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-10-2019, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T10:50:50-08:00","id":1286488,"title":"","content":"Again, some charmsets are better than others, but that's certainly the case for combat abilities (and Presence. Performance is slightly better than Presence, but not hugely).<br /> <br /> Whereas all of my Occult charms actually<i> do </i>something, or upgrade another charm permanently (so I can just write them combined on my character sheet). Most of my Investigation charms do, as well (the others are Double 8s once/scene, and a free excellency once/scene. They're pretty easy to combo, and no re-rolls are involved, so it doesn't slow things down. Actually the free excellency marginally speeds things up).<br /> <br /> Of course, combat is the point at which you have to work out how to combine your charms the quickest.<br /> <br /> I think Martial Arts are not as bad as the main combat abilities. I do have to think a bit about how to combine my different Tiger Style charms, but not too much, they're fairly straightforward, and are mostly used for different stuff. I don't know how others have found it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-10-2019, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T04:31:29-08:00","id":1286662,"title":"","content":"You know what I forgot I hated in this edition, the awful syntax. The construction of the system in the language they used leads to so much confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T04:56:47-08:00","id":1286665,"title":"","content":"I only found that in the Solar charms (which has a number of charms where we argued about the way they worked because of the wording).<br /> Sorcery, martial arts, and the stuff in Arms and DB seems to be written nice and clearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T06:45:53-08:00","id":1286685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286468#post1286468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In previous editions, most of the time moves just let you do something you couldn't do. Sometimes they gave you extra dice but that wasn't always the case. <br /> <br /> In this edition, the charmbloat is insane. You have 4-10x the charms you used to and most of them just seem to add dice. They make you better than normal but they're just a bridge rather than stepping stones to power. Getting the ability to attack twice isn't that great without all the other charms that boost the dice you roll. So you end up forming combos to do optimal damage. In addition,to that they added roll cascades and other tricks which slow combat down. You used to just get bucket of dice frontloaded with an undodgable attack. Now it's pieced out into several different phases on it's own. The new system is somewhat more balanced but it's also more obnoxious to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, yes that\u2019s a problem with the new edition in general, and really a big one with some Solar trees. The DB ones have some of that problem, half have dice tricks built into their excellency, but on the whole I think they\u2019re a lot better. There\u2019s many simple charms that let you do things that you couldn\u2019t before, the signature charms especially.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also it might help that for DBs the ability to attack twice in a turn is worth it on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-11-2019, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T06:47:59-08:00","id":1286686,"title":"","content":"NaTuRaL lAnGuAgE iS tHe FuTuRe<br /> <br /> <br /> But seriously that shit is confusing and I run DB so don'teven need to fiddle with corebook charms. It's still all over the core rules. I think it took me a while longer to parse the social rules than their complexity warranted. Was there ever a full explanation for the call there or was it only ever stylistic, like the idea of not needing an ST chapter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T06:50:35-08:00","id":1286687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286686#post1286686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NaTuRaL lAnGuAgE iS tHe FuTuRe<br /> <br /> <br /> But seriously that shit is confusing and I run DB so don'teven need to fiddle with corebook charms. It's still all over the core rules. I think it took me a while longer to parse the social rules than their complexity warranted. Was there ever a full explanation for the call there or was it only ever stylistic, like the idea of not needing an ST chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want a DMG for exalted so bad. That and/or a lot more published adventures so that I can see how a lot of this stuff is meant to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T06:58:46-08:00","id":1286690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286687#post1286687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want a DMG for exalted so bad. That and/or a lot more published adventures so that I can see how a lot of this stuff is meant to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>A softback storyteller guide is apparently happening. A lot of those books happen in the in between space with the big books so no idea how long it'll take to get here but it'll come along in time. Hoping sooner than later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:33:59-08:00","id":1286702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286690#post1286690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A softback storyteller guide is apparently happening. A lot of those books happen in the in between space with the big books so no idea how long it'll take to get here but it'll come along in time. Hoping sooner than later</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that will be a blessing. The DnD DMG is actually very helpful in a lot of ways, especially when it comes to giving an expectation of what kind of things can/should be happening in the game. So has looking at published materials, which are varied but also full of ideas that made me go \u201cahhh so that\u2019s how that\u2019s supposed to work.\u201d <br /> <br /> Reading through exalted adventures tends to be twice as insightful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:55:43-08:00","id":1286705,"title":"","content":"Mostly I find the DMG a waste of time (I used it like twice in my last game, for magic items), but in some ways Exalted is a harder game to run; characters are less balanced in terms of combat, there's no Challenge Rating, etc. There's also a lot more ST adjudication, for example sorcerous workings. So I can see the value there, and I know Vance and Minton are very keen on doing one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:09:06-08:00","id":1286712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286686#post1286686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NaTuRaL lAnGuAgE iS tHe FuTuRe<br /> <br /> <br /> But seriously that shit is confusing and I run DB so don'teven need to fiddle with corebook charms. It's still all over the core rules. I think it took me a while longer to parse the social rules than their complexity warranted. Was there ever a full explanation for the call there or was it only ever stylistic, like the idea of not needing an ST chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Partly, John Morke never was much one for concise text.<br /> <br /> But mostly, from what I understand, it's because the text got leaked, and so near the end the final text was heavily restricted to a small number of people, which did not include the guy who was supposed to edit it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:22:31-08:00","id":1286717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286712#post1286712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> which did not include the guy who was supposed to edit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't weirdly paranoid and somewhat crazy at all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:28:47-08:00","id":1286721,"title":"","content":"Could we get some kind of kickstarter for an errata going, so that Robert Vance can actually get PAID to clarify and/or fix the corebook rules and content?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:33:05-08:00","id":1286723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286705#post1286705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I find the DMG a waste of time (I used it like twice in my last game, for magic items), but in some ways Exalted is a harder game to run; characters are less balanced in terms of combat, there's no Challenge Rating, etc. There's also a lot more ST adjudication, for example sorcerous workings. So I can see the value there, and I know Vance and Minton are very keen on doing one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh really? That\u2019s fascinating, I\u2019ve used it for everything from finding out how much it costs to build a castle to what exactly are the in-game effects when a character spends 3 straight months carousing. Also alternate healing and spell regeneration rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s kind of what I\u2019d want out of exalted, examples or guidelines on what exactly the leadership system can do, even if that boils down to \u201chere are three decent ways to run those kind of projects.\u201d Or you might have a section on how to properly use battlegroups, like for instance how a group of 4 bodyguards should be run as a size 1 BG otherwise they\u2019re way more of a liability than a benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:33:50-08:00","id":1286724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286717#post1286717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't weirdly paranoid and somewhat crazy at all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he was one of those who could have leaked it (I don't think he did, but how would I know), so I can kind of understand why they did it... But the charms section really could have done with an external editor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:44:14-08:00","id":1286729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286275#post1286275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do a bit, but at level 4 I don't have a ton of options*. Sometimes I levitate enemies, but then the combat characters can't reach them. Also, one of the girls in the group is playing a bard, and she does a lot of buffing/debuffing/battlefield control (sleep, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah gotcha, yeah give it a few levels and see how it changes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286275#post1286275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the game doesn't support social characters with many interesting things to do besides &quot;have a high skill rating&quot;. Princess Evylyn rolls high rolls for diplomacy, Xenophon (my wizard) gets high rolls for knowledge, and Blaze rolls high for stealth and theft, but the game doesn't give us much to do with that beyond the skill checks. That's where Exalted stands out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:49:27-08:00","id":1286731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286729#post1286729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Completely agree</div> </div> </div> </div>I also agree. I also find that the heavy combat focus of the current game is a detriment to the game. Arms of the chosen was what 80% of the books, it was a huge waste IMO. Combat has personally been the most boring part of the game for me and to emphasize it more seems like a waste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T09:00:42-08:00","id":1286734,"title":"","content":"I loved Arms, it had a lot of cool lore and ideas in the evocation mechanics that are helping me out as a GM when it comes to figuring out ways to pair desired effects and themes. <br /> <br /> That post he was replying too was specifically about the encounter focused nature of Dungeons and Dragons compared to Exalted having actual social investment anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T09:18:40-08:00","id":1286743,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was saying DnD doesn't give social characters much to do besides roll a D20 for Persuasion or Deception (or Diplomacy and Bluff in older versions).<br /> <br /> Sure, Arms was mostly combat, but the Core book has lots of social charms (though I think the DB social charms are more interesting; but the point stands for, say, Investigation. My DnD character has +7 Investigation and a couple of Divination spells, but my Zenith can detect lies/scope out a scene in 5 seconds/make people give up a confession/put tiny clues together like Sherlock Holmes/etc).<br /> <br /> Arms... I actually liked Arms too, in terms of lore and ideas. And art, actually.<br /> <br /> I would have preferred a book less focused on combat (say, Dragonblood), but for a book mostly about combat, it was very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-11-2019, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T12:34:18-08:00","id":1286809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286743#post1286743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was saying DnD doesn't give social characters much to do besides roll a D20 for Persuasion or Deception (or Diplomacy and Bluff in older versions).<br /> <br /> Sure, Arms was mostly combat, but the Core book has lots of social charms (though I think the DB social charms are more interesting; but the point stands for, say, Investigation. My DnD character has +7 Investigation and a couple of Divination spells, but my Zenith can detect lies/scope out a scene in 5 seconds/make people give up a confession/put tiny clues together like Sherlock Holmes/etc).<br /> <br /> Arms... I actually liked Arms too, in terms of lore and ideas. And art, actually.<br /> <br /> I would have preferred a book less focused on combat (say, Dragonblood), but for a book mostly about combat, it was very good.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is that i feel like combat gets too much of a focus and arms was terrible at showing non-combat artifacts. The emphasis on combat in 3e is rather absurd. Which is where my opinion of exalted compared to d&amp;d comes in because D&amp;D felt like a combat heavy game that works. Whereas exalted excelled at storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T12:47:17-08:00","id":1286813,"title":"","content":"I'm going to counter that this is the first edition with a social system I have ever invested thought in as well as the combat rules. 2e was kind of a mess that hurt my brain when you started cutting into its rules there. <br /> <br /> Exalted is definitely loaded with combat options and items of course, not disputing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T13:36:47-08:00","id":1286829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286809#post1286809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem is that i feel like combat gets too much of a focus and arms was terrible at showing non-combat artifacts. The emphasis on combat in 3e is rather absurd. Which is where my opinion of exalted compared to d&amp;d comes in because D&amp;D felt like a combat heavy game that works. Whereas exalted excelled at storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to make a little distinction here, something getting more raw wordcount then something else doesn't mean the smaller thing isnt important, so long as it gets the material it does need.<br /> <br /> To use an example, the actual investigation rules are quite simplistic. They amount to about a page total and only really include profile character and case scene, but that's all they really need. That little mechanical framework is all you actually need to build fleshed out investigation and larceny charm sets. You can still play the detective character and have fun toys to play with when you do.<br /> <br /> So yes combat has more word count dedicated to it (mainly because the consequences of combat are so much more severe then an investigation scene or anything else) but I don't see how that in any way detracts from the fact that there is indeed a full charm set for these other things out there for you to build a character around","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T14:53:44-08:00","id":1286852,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, while combat trees have more charms than non-combat trees (except Craft), the proportion I think is actually better than 2nd ed. In 2nd ed, quite a few of the Twilight, Night and Eclipse charm trees literally had, not counting excellencies, 5 charms. 5. That's less than a Martial Art.<br /> So, while combat still has more, I feel the balance is actually better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:40:59-08:00","id":1286896,"title":"","content":"I'm of two minds in response to the comment about Arms.<br /> <br /> One is that the nature of the magic of a lot of the things in the first part is that, while their concepts are applied through the lens of combat, many of them clearly have wide applications beyond combat, from the Distaff's use in healing, crafting and entangling, up to the Forgotten Blade cultivating memories like a bonsai.<br /> <br /> The other mind is sympathetic to the argument that such applications lend themselves to divesting the Artifacts of combat applications altogether, although personally I've developed a fondness for the sense that a lot of those things take the role of ceremonial weapons to represent various kinds of task or office, that remain perfectly functional as weapons.<br /> <br /> Either way, the depth, nuance and creativity on display there, producing the most compelling magical items in anything ever, hardly make the effort wasted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T18:40:59-08:00","id":1286930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286809#post1286809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem is that i feel like combat gets too much of a focus and arms was terrible at showing non-combat artifacts. The emphasis on combat in 3e is rather absurd. Which is where my opinion of exalted compared to d&amp;d comes in because D&amp;D felt like a combat heavy game that works. Whereas exalted excelled at storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of this. I love the content in Arms. LOVE it. Find all of the fluff MUCH more interesting than any of the Core artifacts except maybe Volcano Cutter and got great ideas for creating the stories of Artifacts in general. Even so, and even with the overall removal of Magitech, I did want to see more non-combat Artifacts. I get they're not as &quot;sexy&quot; since they are unlike to call forth Evocations, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T18:52:02-08:00","id":1286936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286930#post1286930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with all of this. I love the content in Arms. LOVE it. Find all of the fluff MUCH more interesting than any of the Core artifacts except maybe Volcano Cutter and got great ideas for creating the stories of Artifacts in general. Even so, and even with the overall removal of Magitech, I did want to see more non-combat Artifacts. I get they're not as &quot;sexy&quot; since they are unlike to call forth Evocations, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noncombat artifacts should still have evocations. My biggest issue is that there are no noncombat artifacts that have a good set of evocations when there is nothing preventing that. It's hard to judge how to make them that when the only thing we get are weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T19:06:14-08:00","id":1286944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286936#post1286936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noncombat artifacts should still have evocations. My biggest issue is that there are no noncombat artifacts that have a good set of evocations when there is nothing preventing that. It's hard to judge how to make them that when the only thing we get are weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>No love for Wings of the Raptor, I see.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T22:58:21-08:00","id":1286978,"title":"","content":"Wings of the Raptor is cool. I also liked those drums that controlled hungry ghosts.<br /> <br /> There are non-combat artefacts, though they have quite short evocation trees.<br /> And, as Isator mentioned, there are magic weapons with non-combat evocations; the Distaff and Asphodel spring to mind.<br /> <br /> Still, I'd estimate that 75-90% of the evocations are for combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T00:07:28-08:00","id":1286988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286936#post1286936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Noncombat artifacts should still have evocations. My biggest issue is that there are no noncombat artifacts that have a good set of evocations when there is nothing preventing that. It's hard to judge how to make them that when the only thing we get are weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a whole chapter with several of those. There is a prosthetic arm whose legend provides it with powers of self-actualisation and self-reliance. There are running shoes whose legend flows into powers of chasing after loved ones in distress. There is a drum to control hungry ghosts, evolving into harnessing them within still living bodies. The Wings of the Raptor uses Evocations as the model for developing increasing mastery of their power of flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T07:30:15-08:00","id":1287047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284756-third-edition-in-retrospect-thus-far?p=1286988#post1286988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a whole chapter with several of those. There is a prosthetic arm whose legend provides it with powers of self-actualisation and self-reliance. There are running shoes whose legend flows into powers of chasing after loved ones in distress. There is a drum to control hungry ghosts, evolving into harnessing them within still living bodies. The Wings of the Raptor uses Evocations as the model for developing increasing mastery of their power of flight.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are very few and far between and none of them got remotely as detailed or as intricate as combat artifacts. Almost all the weapons individually had more word count devoted to them than all the non-combat weapons combined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T11:26:08-08:00","id":1287134,"title":"","content":"I do really like how AotC (especially) reveals a much more complex history and many turnings of many ages.<br /> <br /> On the downside, the Core book is really hard to read through, because a lot of text that should be highlighted for quick reference isn't, or blends in with the prose around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T11:33:43-08:00","id":1287144,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the periodisation of the artefacts is really nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T19:44:26-08:00","id":1288148,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, coming back with one thing I just remembered<br /> Con: I don't like the excessive use of quick characters. Like the book itself says, they're good for characters who are going to appear in passing, who aren't going to be on focus very much, and I fully understand that they're much simpler to write and less hassle, but now they're getting used for big characters to. I'd really prefer people like Mnemon or the Roseblack or even the upcoming lunar elders get full stat blocks rather then just lists of dice pools and sample charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:09:42-08:00","id":1288482,"title":"","content":"The pros of Ex3 in my book are:<br /> <br /> - Amazing battle system and mechanics. While DnD is easier (dunno how much easier, but easier) it has a lot of stuff that is just boring or downright annoying. After we got used to the system (especially I as the ST) battles also weren't that much slower than in Ex2 (and sometimes even DnD battles take a comparable amount of time).<br /> - Best social system I know of. Even more so after seeing the &quot;systems&quot; of other RPGs. I don't think I'll be STing a game again that does not have a homebrewed version of intimacies. Did so for DnD and is so much better than before.<br /> - Artifacts have the potential to be the coolest magical items I know of.<br /> - The new map and the additions to the setting. I even wrote a personal setting that plays on the ground of the Dreaming Sea.<br /> - Charms. While yes, there are a lot of them, they also enable very specific character builds and add a lot of variety. You rarely overshoot your intended power level by much by just buying a single charm.<br /> - Solar Xp is awesome.<br /> - The improvements to sorcery. I adore the initiations.<br /> - Trauma Bear.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully positive, but that will be future stuff:<br /> - Great potential for mixed circles. In the other editions there were so many problems with the systems and charms that a mixed circle felt very daunting. I think Ex3 has the best chance of making it not only possible without much houseruling, but also to make it fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> - Lack of material. The number 1 reason we stopped playing. With a Monster Manual like book we probably would still be playing. In the end I was burned out on homebrewing everying.<br /> - The amount of work needed to run (and to a lesser extend to play) the game. I realized very late in my STing the kind of story a group of Solars requires, since there wasn't much of a guideline available. This is something I realize the more I play other RPGs. You can do a lot of things in Exalted but because of that you as the ST are limited in some factors that other RPGs don't.<br /> My friend had a lot of problems with this, because as the ST he kept introducing special powers for the enemies to play with, which is cool. But after we dealt with them, he misjudged the applicabilty of our Charms/Sorcery which would either allow us to reproduce said power in some way, simply aquire it, or learn it some way. So he was forced to explain why we couldn't do it, even though our powers outright said we could. This in turn warped his story in a way he didn't wanted to and we as players were always questioning if our course of action would lead to more weird and frustrating developments when we were using our powers a bit outside of the box. A &quot;How to build a high magic storyline with almost omnipowerful demigods as protagonists without loosing sight of their very human core&quot; Section in the corebook would have helped a big deal.<br /> - The lack of balancing guidelines and help. This is for homebrew charms/artifacts/etc. but also for enemies. The amount of time I spend to get a feel for balacing encounters for my player group was very disheartening. This was also the main reason my friend stopped STing. It was just too much work and there were too many frustrating moments for him because he misjudged the power levels of his group and/or his encounters.<br /> - The Crafting Charmset for Solars. The basic system is fine and fun, but the charmset is boring, costly, extremely complex and very difficult to adequately consider as a ST (how many materials should be given? How much downtime should be allowed? When is it good for downtime to occur?).<br /> - While sorcery is the best it ever was, playing a &quot;Sorceror&quot; as a Solar Exalted is very underwhelming because of very few charms that interact with sorcery at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Things that stayed the same:<br /> - Still extremely difficult to find German groups to play Exalted with.<br /> - Battles are a real committment.<br /> - The system requires a LOT of communication between basically everyone outside of the game because of all the options the system offers. Maybe this edition even more than the previous ones.<br /> - Solars are still badass.<br /> <br /> <br /> All in all: Exalted 3 is not without flaws, but it is the best RPG I have played up until now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}